      "comment": "Initializes all core subsystems required for the Diablo II Game Server to start and run.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize logging system with \"D2GSInit\" category\n2. Log server startup message with server name \"Diablo II Game Server\"\n3. Initialize MPQ (archive) system - critical for game data access\n4. Initialize language localization system\n5. Configure data pre-caching based on server settings\n6. Initialize game data tables (items, spells, etc.)\n7. Configure NT-specific features if enabled (priority scheduling)\n8. Initialize network listening socket for client connections\n9. Set up callback function table for game event handling\n10. Finalize initialization and mark server as ready\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global configuration settings\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success: All subsystems initialized successfully, server ready\n0 - Failure: One or more critical subsystems failed to initialize\n\nError Codes (via SetLastError):\n0x10000002 - Failed to initialize callback function table\n0x10000003 - MPQ system initialization failed\n0x10000004 - Language system initialization failed  \n0x10000007 - Network initialization failed\n\nNotes:\nThis is the main entry point for server startup\nFailure at any step will abort initialization and return 0\nNT priority scheduling uses values: 100, 200, 300, 400\nAll initialization steps are logged via D2GSInit category",
