      "comment": "Main game server execution loop that processes game logic and handles messages until shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter main processing loop while shutdown flag is clear (g_pGameServerState + 8 == 0)\n2. Update current tick timestamp with GetTickCount()\n3. Execute game processing handler callback (g_pfnGameProcessHandler)\n4. Update tick timestamp and call game update function FUN_680058c0\n5. Update tick timestamp and process incoming messages with message processor callback\n6. Branch based on message processing result:\n   - If no messages processed: Clear tick counter, sleep for idle interval (offset 0x28)\n   - If messages processed: Update tick, call shutdown handler, clear tick, sleep for active interval (offset 0x2c)\n7. Return to step 2 until shutdown condition is met\n8. On shutdown: Update final tick timestamp, call cleanup handler\n9. Call shutdown handler with exit flag (1, 0) and return success code\n\nParameters:\nNone - void function taking no parameters\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 indicating successful completion of main loop\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Sleep intervals are configurable via g_pGameServerState structure offsets:\n  - Offset 0x28: Idle sleep duration when no messages processed\n  - Offset 0x2c: Active sleep duration when messages were processed\n- Function callbacks are configurable via global function pointers:\n  - g_pfnGameProcessHandler: Main game logic processor\n  - g_pfnMessageProcessor: Network message handler  \n  - g_pfnShutdownHandler: Cleanup operations (called twice with different parameters)\n  - g_pfnCleanupHandler: Final resource cleanup\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8: Offset to shutdown flag in game server state structure\n- 0x28: Offset to idle sleep interval in milliseconds\n- 0x2c: Offset to active sleep interval in milliseconds\n- 1: Exit parameter passed to shutdown handler indicating normal termination",
