      "comment": "Initiates orderly shutdown sequence for D2 Game Server and releases system resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Log shutdown initiation message with shutdown flag parameter to debug handler\n2. Execute sequential cleanup function pointer chain (6 functions) with result chaining\n3. Call specialized component cleanup function (FUN_68002880)\n4. Call additional server cleanup operations (InitializeServerCleanup)\n5. Check if DLL module list exists and iterate through array to unload modules\n6. For each DLL: get module handle, free library, advance to next entry\n7. Call final resource cleanup function (FUN_680024f0)\n8. Log shutdown completion message with final result to debug handler\n9. Return success status constant (0x1)\n\nParameters:\ndwShutdownFlag (uint): Shutdown mode flag passed to logging functions for debug identification\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success) - function performs best-effort cleanup without error propagation\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf DLL module list is NULL (PTR_s_D2Client_dll_6800d040), DLL unloading step is skipped.\nCleanup functions are called unconditionally regardless of previous step failures.\nResult chaining allows each cleanup function to receive output from previous operation.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1: Success return code indicating shutdown sequence completed\n0x0: NULL check value for DLL array termination and function parameter\n\nError Handling:\nFunction performs fire-and-forget cleanup - errors from individual steps do not halt sequence.\nGetModuleHandleA and FreeLibrary failures are ignored to ensure complete cleanup attempt.\nNo validation of function pointer validity before calls (assumes proper initialization).",
