      "comment": "Initialize server cleanup subsystem and prepare for shutdown\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate server handle by calling cleanup function with server handle and mode 1\n2. If validation fails (returns false), exit early with failure status\n3. Call primary cleanup routine to deallocate resources\n4. Call cleanup function with cleanup handle and mode 1 to prepare secondary cleanup\n5. Call final cleanup routine to complete resource deallocation\n6. Set shutdown flag to 0 to indicate clean shutdown state\n7. Return success status\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\ntrue - Cleanup initialization succeeded, server ready for shutdown\nfalse - Cleanup initialization failed, server handle invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (decimal 1) - Cleanup mode parameter for validation/preparation calls\n\nError Handling:\n- Early return on server handle validation failure\n- No error propagation from subsequent cleanup calls\n- Assumes all cleanup functions after validation will succeed",
