      "comment": "Parses a comma-separated parameter string to find pattern matches in a target buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (pTargetBuffer and lpszParameterString not null)\n2. Get target buffer size using GetPEOptionalHeaderSize from DOS header\n3. Split parameter string by comma delimiter to extract offset and hex pattern\n4. Validate exactly 2 parameters were provided (base offset and hex pattern)\n5. Parse first parameter as base offset using strtoul with base auto-detection\n6. Calculate hex pattern string length using manual string scan\n7. Allocate memory for pattern entry array based on hex string length\n8. Convert hex string to byte pattern using ParseHexStringToBytes\n9. Search target buffer for pattern match using FindPatternInBuffer\n10. Free allocated pattern memory and parameter token array\n11. Return absolute offset (pattern match offset + base offset) or 0 if no match\n\nParameters:\n  pTargetBuffer - Pointer to target buffer to search (cast from IMAGE_DOS_HEADER*)\n  lpszParameterString - Comma-separated parameter string \"offset,hexpattern\"\n\nReturns:\n  Absolute offset where pattern was found (base offset + match offset)\n  0 if input validation failed or pattern not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Parameter string must contain exactly 2 comma-separated values\n  Hex pattern string is manually scanned for length calculation\n  Pattern memory allocation size: ((hex_string_length - 1) / 2) * 4 bytes\n  Base offset parsed as decimal/hex (0x prefix) or octal (0 prefix)",
