      "comment": "Searches for the first occurrence of a pattern within a buffer range using sliding window approach\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (buffer size and pattern count must be non-zero)\n2. Calculate maximum search range (dwSearchRange = dwBufferSize - dwPatternCount)\n3. Check if search is possible (dwBufferSize != dwPatternCount)\n4. Initialize search position counter (dwCurrentOffset = 0)\n5. Loop through buffer positions:\n   a. Call pattern matching function at current position (nBufferBase + dwCurrentOffset)\n   b. If pattern matches, return found position (dwCurrentOffset + nBufferBase)\n   c. If no match, increment position and continue\n   d. If search range exhausted, return 0 (not found)\n6. Return 0 if no search needed or pattern not found\n\nParameters:\nnBufferBase     - int: Base address/offset of buffer to search within\ndwBufferSize    - uint: Total size of searchable buffer in bytes\npPatternArray   - PatternEntry *: Array of pattern entries (value+mask pairs)\ndwPatternCount  - uint: Number of pattern entries to match sequentially\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Position offset where pattern was found (nBufferBase + offset)\nFailure: 0 if pattern not found or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 immediately if dwBufferSize or dwPatternCount is 0\n- Returns nBufferBase if dwBufferSize equals dwPatternCount (no sliding needed)\n- Pattern matching uses value+mask comparison for each entry\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n-------|------|------------|--------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 1    | bValue     | byte   | Expected byte value for pattern match\n0x01   | 1    | bMask      | byte   | Bit mask applied during comparison\n0x02   | 2    | wPadding   | ushort | Padding to align to 4-byte boundary",
