      "comment": "Validates a sequence of byte patterns against a data buffer using mask-based comparison\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize pattern index to 0\n2. If pattern count is 0, return success (1)\n3. For each pattern entry in the array:\n   - Load byte from data buffer at current index\n   - Apply mask from pattern entry (offset +1) to data byte\n   - Compare masked result with comparison byte (offset +0)\n   - If match fails, return failure (0)\n   - Increment pattern index and advance pattern pointer by 4 bytes\n   - Continue until all patterns processed\n4. Return success (1) if all patterns match\n\nParameters:\n\n- pDataBuffer: Pointer to data buffer being validated\n- pPatternArray: Array of PatternEntry structures containing comparison and mask bytes\n- nPatternCount: Number of pattern entries to process\n\nReturns:\n\n- 1: All patterns match successfully\n- 0: Pattern validation failed\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nPatternEntry (4 bytes):\n| Offset | Size | Field Name       | Type | Description                    |\n|--------|------|------------------|------|--------------------------------|\n| 0x00   | 1    | comparisonByte   | byte | Expected value after masking   |\n| 0x01   | 1    | maskByte         | byte | Bit mask applied to data byte  |\n| 0x02   | 1    | reserved1        | byte | Unused padding byte            |\n| 0x03   | 1    | reserved2        | byte | Unused padding byte            |\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Empty pattern array (nPatternCount == 0) returns success without processing\n- Pattern validation stops at first mismatch and returns failure\n- Each pattern entry occupies 4 bytes regardless of actual data used",
