      "instructions": ["0x2090|SUB|ESP, 0xc", "0x2093|PUSH|ESI", "0x2094|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x2098|PUSH|EDI", "0x2099|MOV|EDI, ESI", "0x209B|OR|ECX, 0xffffffff", "0x209E|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x20A0|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x20A2|SCASB.REPNE|ES:EDI", "0x20A4|NOT|ECX", "0x20A6|DEC|ECX", "0x20A7|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x20A9|CMP|ECX, EDX", "0x20AB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDX", "0x20AF|MOV|byte ptr [ESP + 0xa], DL"],
      "comment": "Converts hexadecimal string representation to byte array with whitespace skipping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate input string length using REPNE SCASB instruction\n2. Return 0 immediately if string length is zero or negative\n3. Initialize loop counters and temporary storage variables\n4. Enter main character processing loop iterating through each character\n5. Skip whitespace characters (spaces 0x20 and tabs 0x09) by advancing pointer\n6. For non-whitespace characters, extract 2-character hex substring using strncpy\n7. Convert hex substring to unsigned long using strtoul with base 16\n8. Check conversion success by examining endptr from strtoul\n9. If conversion successful (endptr NULL or points to null terminator):\n   - Store converted byte value in output array with high byte set to 0xFF\n10. If conversion failed (endptr points to unconverted characters):\n    - Store 0x00000000 in output array to indicate parse error\n11. Increment all counters: source pointer, output pointer, byte count\n12. Continue loop until all characters processed\n13. Return final byte count as function result\n\nParameters:\nlpszHexString (char *): Input string containing hexadecimal digits and optional whitespace\npdwOutput (uint *): Output array to store converted bytes as 32-bit values\n\nReturns:\nint: Number of bytes successfully parsed and stored in output array\n     Returns 0 if input string is empty or NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Whitespace characters (space 0x20, tab 0x09) are skipped without advancing output\n- Each valid hex byte stored as 32-bit value with high byte 0xFF, low byte parsed value\n- Invalid hex characters result in 0x00000000 stored in output array\n- Function processes pairs of hex digits but advances source pointer by 1 each iteration\n- Empty or zero-length input strings return immediately with result 0",
