      "comment": "Process game object entries by setting or clearing flag bits based on mask filter\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if object array is initialized (first entry ID not -1)\n2. Skip to first entry at offset 0x18 from array base\n3. For each entry in the array:\n   a. Check if entry matches filter criteria (mask filter 0xFFFFFFFF = all, or entry mask & filter != 0)\n   b. If match found, modify entry flags:\n      - If nOperation == 0: Set bit 2 (0x4) in flags field\n      - If nOperation != 0: Clear bit 2 (0x4) in flags field\n   c. Increment processed count\n   d. Advance to next entry (stride = 0x2C = 44 bytes)\n   e. Continue until next entry ID field == 0xFFFFFFFF (terminator)\n4. Return count of processed entries\n\nParameters:\npObjectArray - Pointer to array of GameObjectEntry structures\ndwMaskFilter - Bit mask for filtering entries (0xFFFFFFFF = process all entries)\nnOperation - Operation type: 0 = set flag bit, non-zero = clear flag bit\n\nReturns:\nint - Number of entries that matched filter and were processed\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------------|------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwFlags          | uint | Object flags (bit 2 = processing state)\n0x04   | 4    | dwMask          | uint | Entry mask for filter matching\n0x08   | 4    | field_0x8       | uint | Unknown field\n0x0C   | 4    | field_0xc       | uint | Unknown field\n0x10   | 4    | field_0x10      | uint | Unknown field\n0x14   | 4    | dwNextEntryId   | uint | Next entry ID (0xFFFFFFFF = end)\n0x18   | 4    | field_0x18      | uint | Unknown field\n0x1C   | 4    | field_0x1c      | uint | Unknown field\n0x20   | 4    | field_0x20      | uint | Unknown field\n0x24   | 4    | field_0x24      | uint | Unknown field\n0x28   | 4    | field_0x28      | uint | Unknown field\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24) - Offset to first entry in array\n0x2C (44) - Size of each GameObjectEntry structure\n0x4 (4) - Flag bit being set/cleared (bit 2)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Terminator value and \"process all\" mask filter\n0xFFFFFFFB - Bit mask for clearing bit 2 (AND operation)",
