      "comment": "Process server handle counters by decrementing reference counts.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first server handle entry from g_pServerHandle array\n2. Check if handle is valid (not 0xFFFFFFFF sentinel value)\n3. Initialize offset counter to traverse array entries\n4. For each valid server handle entry:\n   a. Calculate pointer to counter field at offset +4 from entry base\n   b. Call string lookup function to get decrement value for handle name\n   c. Subtract lookup value from existing counter at offset +4\n   d. Advance offset by 0x2C bytes (44-byte structure stride)\n   e. Load next handle entry pointer\n5. Continue loop until reaching sentinel value 0xFFFFFFFF\n6. Return when all entries processed\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global g_pServerHandle array\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies counter values in place\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type     Description\n------  ----  ----------------  -------  --------------------------\n0x00    4     pszHandleName     char*    Server handle identifier string\n0x04    4     dwCounterValue    uint     Reference counter (decremented)\n0x08    36    reserved          byte[36] Padding/reserved fields\nTotal: 44 bytes (0x2C stride)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty array: If first entry is 0xFFFFFFFF, function returns immediately\n- String lookup miss: If FUN_680021b0 returns 0, counter unchanged\n- Counter underflow: No bounds checking on subtraction operation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF - Sentinel value marking end of server handle array\n0x2C (44)  - Size of each ServerHandleEntry structure\n0x4        - Offset to dwCounterValue field within structure",
