      "comment": "Releases memory allocated for the patch fog pool buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global buffer pointer from g_pvAllocatedBuffer\n2. Test if buffer pointer is non-null\n3. If null, skip cleanup and proceed to step 6\n4. Call VirtualFree with buffer pointer, size 0, and MEM_RELEASE flag (0x8000)\n5. Clear global buffer pointer by setting g_pvAllocatedBuffer to NULL\n6. Return success status (TRUE)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters, operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nTRUE (1) - Memory cleanup completed successfully\nFunction always returns TRUE regardless of whether cleanup was needed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If buffer pointer is already NULL, function safely returns without action\n- Uses VirtualFree with MEM_RELEASE (0x8000) to fully deallocate virtual memory\n- Pairs with memory allocation performed in related allocator function\n- Safe to call multiple times due to null pointer check\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8000 - MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree API call (releases entire allocation)\n0x0 - NULL value used to clear buffer pointer after deallocation\n1 - TRUE return value indicating successful completion\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling - VirtualFree return value is ignored\nFunction assumes successful deallocation in all cases",
