      "comment": "Copy global log handler function pointer to backup location\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the current log handler function pointer from g_pfnLogHandler global\n2. Store the pointer value into g_pfnLogHandlerCopy for backup/restoration\n3. Set return value to 1 to indicate successful copy operation\n4. Return to caller with success status\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 to indicate successful copy operation\n       - Success: 1 (pointer copy completed successfully)\n       - Never fails as operation is simple memory copy\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function always succeeds as it performs simple pointer copy\n  - No validation performed on pointer values (NULL or invalid pointers copied as-is)\n  - Both source and destination are global memory locations\n  - Operation is atomic at assembly level\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1 - Success return code indicating pointer copy completed\n  0x6800d7d0 - Address of g_pfnLogHandler source global\n  0x68010f00 - Address of g_pfnLogHandlerCopy destination global",
