      "comment": "Configures import link table based on application version range\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Mask input version to 28 bits (dwVersion & 0x0FFFFFFF)\n2. Check if masked version < 0x1000700 (version 16.7.0)\n3. If version >= 0x1000700: Set import table to high version table at 0x6800E518\n4. If version < 0x1000700 but > 0x0FFFFFF: Set import table to low version table at 0x6800E4A8\n5. If version <= 0x0FFFFFF: No table assignment (use existing/default)\n6. Return success status (always 1)\n\nParameters:\ndwVersion (uint): Application version encoded as 32-bit value, upper 4 bits ignored\n\nReturns:\n1 (uint): Success status (function always succeeds)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVersion ranges:\n- 0x0000000-0x0FFFFFF: No import table change (legacy/fallback behavior)  \n- 0x1000000-0x10006FF: Uses import table at 0x6800E4A8 (PTR_g_hD2WinLibrary_6800e4a8)\n- 0x1000700+: Uses import table at 0x6800E518 (PTR_g_hD2WinLibrary_6800e518)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0FFFFFFF (268435455): Version mask removes upper 4 bits for range checking\n0x1000000 (16777216): Minimum version for import table assignment (version 16.0.0)  \n0x1000700 (16779008): Version threshold for high vs low import table (version 16.7.0)\n0x6800E728: Global pointer g_pImportLinkTable storage location\n0x6800E4A8: Low version import function table (PTR_g_hD2WinLibrary_6800e4a8)\n0x6800E518: High version import function table (PTR_g_hD2WinLibrary_6800e518)",
