      "comment": "Installs API hooks by patching import table entries with new function addresses.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - check module pointer, descriptor array, and optional arrays\n2. Count hook descriptors by scanning until 0xFFFFFFFF terminator\n3. Validate output arrays based on hook count using IsBadWritePtr\n4. Validate hook descriptors - check for null names and valid function pointers\n5. Check system compatibility and module address range validity\n6. Initialize output arrays - clear original addresses and hook count\n7. Get import table from target module using helper function\n8. Parse import table entries to find matching exports by name or ordinal\n9. For each import table entry determine if import is by name or ordinal\n10. Search hook descriptors for matching name or ordinal and patch if found\n\nParameters:\nhModuleBase - Handle to target PE module to hook\nlpszModuleName - Pointer to module name string for import table lookup\npdwHookDescriptors - Array of hook descriptors terminated by 0xFFFFFFFF\npdwOriginalAddresses - Optional output array for original import addresses\npnHooksInstalled - Optional output count of successfully installed hooks\n\nReturns:\n1 (TRUE) - All matching hooks installed successfully\n0 (FALSE) - Validation failed, module invalid, or import table parsing error\n\nSpecial Cases:\nHook descriptor format consists of name/ordinal and replacement address pairs\nOrdinal imports have bit 31 set while name imports have bit 31 clear\nMemory protection temporarily changed to PAGE_READWRITE during patching\nError codes 0x57 and 0x06 set for parameter and handle validation failures\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF - Hook descriptor array terminator\n0x80000000 - Ordinal import flag (bit 31 set)\n0x7FFFFFFF - Maximum valid module address threshold\n0x1C - Size of MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION structure\n0x04 - PAGE_READWRITE protection flag for memory patching\n0x57 - ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER (87 decimal)\n0x06 - ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE (6 decimal)",
