      "instructions": ["0x27A0|PUSH|EBX", "0x27A1|PUSH|EBP", "0x27A2|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x27A6|PUSH|ESI", "0x27A7|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x27A9|PUSH|EDI", "0x27AA|JZ|0x6800281f", "0x27AC|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x27B0|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x27B2|JZ|0x6800281f", "0x27B4|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6800b030]", "0x27BA|PUSH|0x40", "0x27BC|PUSH|EDI", "0x27BD|CALL|EBX", "0x27BF|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Find export directory entry by comparing DLL name.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (non-NULL pImageBase and lpszDllName)\n2. Verify image base readability (64 bytes) and check MZ signature (0x5a4d)\n3. Load NT headers from offset [pImageBase + 0x3c] and validate readability (248 bytes)\n4. Verify PE signature (0x4550) in NT headers\n5. Extract export directory RVA from NT headers offset 0x80\n6. Return NULL if no export directory exists\n7. Load first export directory entry name RVA from [exportDir + 0xc]\n8. Loop through export directory entries comparing names:\n   a. Add image base to name RVA to get absolute address\n   b. Compare entry name with target DLL name using lstrcmpiA (case-insensitive)\n   c. If match found, return export directory entry address\n   d. If no match, advance to next entry (add 0x14 to get next entry)\n   e. Continue until name RVA is NULL (end of list)\n9. Return export directory entry address if found, NULL otherwise\n10. On any validation failure, call SetLastErrorEx(87, 1) and return NULL\n\nParameters:\n  pImageBase (HMODULE): Base address of loaded PE image in memory\n  lpszDllName (char *): Target DLL name to search for in export directory\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Pointer to IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_EXPORT structure for matching DLL\n  Failure: NULL - invalid parameters, corrupt PE headers, or DLL name not found\n  Error: Sets last error to 87 (ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER) on validation failures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Export directory entry stride is 0x14 bytes (20 decimal)\n  Name RVAs are relative to image base and must be converted to absolute addresses\n  Search is case-insensitive via lstrcmpiA comparison function\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x5a4d: MZ signature for DOS header\n  0x4550: PE signature for NT headers  \n  0x3c: Offset to NT headers in DOS header\n  0x80: Export directory RVA offset in NT headers\n  0xc: Name RVA offset within export directory entry\n  0x14: Export directory entry size/stride (20 bytes)\n  0x20: Next name RVA offset within entry\n  0x40: DOS header validation size (64 bytes)\n  0xf8: NT headers validation size (248 bytes)\n  87: ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for SetLastErrorEx",
