      "comment": "Determines if the current operating system is a Windows NT-based platform.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local OSVERSIONINFOA structure by zeroing all 148 bytes\n2. Set structure size field to 0x94 (148 bytes) to indicate version info size\n3. Call GetVersionExA to populate structure with OS version information\n4. Validate GetVersionExA call succeeded (non-zero return)\n5. Check if dwPlatformId equals 2 (VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT)\n6. Return true for NT-based platforms (NT/2000/XP), false for Win9x/failure\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nbool - true if OS is Windows NT-based (dwPlatformId == 2), false if Win9x or GetVersionExA failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf GetVersionExA fails, function returns false rather than checking platform ID\nPlatform ID 2 specifically indicates Windows NT family (NT/2000/XP/Vista/7/etc)\nPlatform ID 1 would indicate Windows 95/98/ME family\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x94 (148) - Size of OSVERSIONINFOA structure in bytes\n0x25 (37) - Number of DWORDs to clear (37 * 4 = 148 bytes)\n0x2 - VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT platform identifier constant\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type     Description\n0x00    4     dwOSVersionInfoSize     DWORD    Structure size (must be 148)\n0x04    4     dwMajorVersion          DWORD    Major version number\n0x08    4     dwMinorVersion          DWORD    Minor version number  \n0x0C    4     dwBuildNumber           DWORD    Build number\n0x10    4     dwPlatformId            DWORD    Platform identifier (1=Win9x, 2=NT)\n0x14    128   szCSDVersion            CHAR[128] Service pack string",
      "tags": ["PARAM_0"]
