      "comment": "Processes and dispatches incoming network packets based on packet type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract packet type from first byte of packet data\n2. Validate packet type is within valid range (< 0x67)\n3. Calculate handler table index using packet type * 16 byte stride\n4. Lookup handler information from global tables:\n   - Function pointer at g_apPacketHandlerTable + index\n   - Expected packet size at g_aPacketSizeTable + index  \n   - Handler flags at g_anPacketFlagsTable + index\n5. Validate packet size matches expected size (if not 0 or -1)\n6. Validate connection state using FUN_680068f8\n7. If handler function exists, call it with packet data and size\n8. If handler returns 0 and flags indicate optional, return success\n9. Otherwise call default packet handler FUN_680029b0\n10. If result is 3, format debug packet dump\n11. Return processing result\n\nParameters:\nnConnectionId - Connection/socket identifier (ECX)\nnSecondaryId - Secondary context identifier (EDX) \npbPacketData - Packet data buffer starting with packet type byte\ndwPacketSize - Size of packet data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n0 - Success, packet processed normally\n1 - Error, invalid packet type, size mismatch, or connection failure\n3 - Special logging case, packet dump generated\n\nSpecial Cases:\nInvalid packet type (>= 0x67) logs error and calls default handler\nExpected size 0x0 or 0xFFFFFFFF indicates variable-length packet\nHandler flags determine whether optional processing applies\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x67 - Maximum valid packet type (103 decimal)\n0x10 - Handler table stride (16 bytes per entry)\n0x0 - Variable packet size indicator\n0xFFFFFFFF - Variable packet size indicator  \n0x3 - Special return code triggering packet dump\n\nStructure Layout:\nHandler table entries (16 bytes each):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n+0x0    4     dwExpectedPacketSize uint    Expected packet size (0/-1 = variable)\n+0x4    4     pfnPacketHandler     void*   Function pointer to packet handler\n+0x8    4     nHandlerFlags        int     Processing flags (0 = required, 1 = optional)\n+0xC    4     (unused)            -       Reserved/padding\n\nNote: Function uses 4 decompiler-generated SSA temporaries (pvVar1, uVar2, uVar3, iVar4) \nthat cannot be renamed via API due to internal compiler optimization.",
