      "instructions": ["0x2AD0|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x2AD4|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x2AD6|MOV|AX, word ptr [ECX + 0x9]", "0x2ADA|SUB|EAX, 0x0", "0x2ADD|JZ|0x68002aec", "0x2ADF|SUB|EAX, 0x2", "0x2AE2|JZ|0x68002aec", "0x2AE4|MOV|EAX, 0x3", "0x2AE9|RET|0x8", "0x2AEC|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x2AEE|RET|0x8"],
      "comment": "Validates the status field of a structure to ensure it contains expected values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the 16-bit status field from offset +9 of the input structure\n2. Check if status field equals 0 (valid state)\n3. Check if status field equals 2 (alternate valid state) \n4. If status is neither 0 nor 2, return error code 3\n5. If status is 0 or 2, return success code 0\n\nParameters:\n- pValidationData (int): Pointer to structure containing status field at offset +9\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success - status field contains valid value (0 or 2)\n- 3: Error - status field contains invalid value (not 0 or 2)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only validates specific status values 0 and 2\n- All other status values are considered invalid\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x0: Valid status state (allowed)\n- 0x2: Alternate valid status state (allowed)  \n- 0x3: Error return code (invalid status detected)\n- 0x9: Byte offset to status field in structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n-------|------|------------|--------|-----------------------------\n0x0-0x8| 9    | Unknown    | byte[9]| Unanalyzed structure header\n0x9    | 2    | wStatus    | ushort | Status validation field",
