      "comment": "Validates packet type and routes to appropriate processing function based on packet type field.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract packet type from offset +9 in packet structure\n2. If packet type is 0 (zero type):\n   - Validate context has valid pointer at offset +0x60\n   - Check nested structure at offset +0x20 is null\n   - If valid, proceed to packet processing\n3. If packet type is 1 (entity lookup type):\n   - Call function pointer g_pfnEntityLookupFunction with packet parameter from offset +5\n   - Validate returned entity pointer is not null\n   - Get object from entity pointer at offset +0x14\n   - Validate object pointer is not null\n   - Compare object ID at offset +0xc with context ID at offset +0xc\n   - Check object has valid name (char at offset +0x44 not null)\n   - Verify entity status at offset +0x10 equals 1 (active)\n   - Validate context pointer at offset +0x60 and nested structure at +0x20\n   - Call processing function with packet parameter twice (pPacket, pPacket)\n4. If packet type is 4 (parameter type):\n   - Call processing function with packet and packet parameter\n5. Any other packet type returns error code 3\n\nParameters:\ndwUnusedParam - Unused parameter passed in ECX register\npContext - GameContext structure with validation fields at +0x60, +0xc\npPacket - PacketHeader structure with type field at +9 and parameter at +5  \ndwPacketParam - Additional packet parameter for type 4 processing\n\nReturns:\n3 - Validation failed or unsupported packet type\nSuccess code from FUN_680029b0 - Result from packet processing function\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPacket type 1 requires entity lookup validation through g_pfnEntityLookupFunction\nPacket types 0 and 1 both require context validation before processing\nPacket type 4 uses different parameter passing to processing function\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0 (0x00) - Zero packet type requiring context validation only\n1 (0x01) - Entity lookup packet type requiring full validation chain  \n3 (0x03) - Error return code for all validation failures\n4 (0x04) - Parameter packet type with simplified validation\n9 (0x09) - Offset to packet type field in packet structure\n5 (0x05) - Offset to packet parameter field in packet structure",
