      "comment": "Validates buffer size and processes buffer data through two-stage validation and operation pipeline.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate minimum buffer size requirement (dwBufferSize >= 4 bytes)\n2. Return error code 1 if buffer too small for processing\n3. Call FUN_68005270 to validate buffer bounds at offset +3 with reduced size\n4. Return error code 1 if bounds validation fails (negative result)\n5. Call ValidateColonPrefixAndProcess to perform main buffer processing operation\n6. Return 0 for successful processing, 2 for processing failure\n\nParameters:\nhContext1 - First context handle passed to processing function\nhContext2 - Second context handle passed to processing function  \nlpszBuffer - Pointer to buffer data to be validated and processed\ndwBufferSize - Size of buffer in bytes (minimum 4 bytes required)\n\nReturns:\n0 - Processing completed successfully\n1 - Validation failed (buffer too small or bounds check failed)\n2 - Main processing operation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer offset +3 used for both validation and processing, suggesting 3-byte header\nValidation performed on reduced buffer (size-3) starting at buffer+3 offset\nReturn value uses bitwise operations to convert boolean to 0/2 result codes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x03 (3) - Header size offset for buffer validation and processing\n0x04 (4) - Minimum buffer size requirement for valid processing",
