      "comment": "Validates whether a comparison value exceeds the threshold of 9.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load comparison value from byte at offset 1 of input structure\n2. Compare loaded value with threshold constant 9\n3. Use SBB instruction to generate -1 if value > 9, 0 if value <= 9\n4. Apply bitwise AND with 3 to mask result to 0 or 3\n5. Return masked result as validation status code\n\nParameters:\n- pCompareData: Pointer to ComparisonData structure containing comparison value\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Value is within acceptable range (value <= 9)\n- 3: Value exceeds threshold (value > 9)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Threshold value 9 is hardcoded magic number for validation boundary\n- Return values are specifically 0 and 3, not boolean true/false\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x9: Threshold comparison value\n- 0x3: Bitmask applied to result (ensures only values 0 or 3 returned)\n- 0x1: Structure offset to access comparison value byte\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|------|---------------------------\n0x0    | 1    | bField0         | byte | First byte (unused by function)\n0x1    | 1    | bCompareValue   | byte | Value compared against threshold",
