      "comment": "Validates that string data starts with colon prefix and delegates processing to specialized handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if data pointer is non-null\n2. Check if string is non-empty (first character not null terminator)\n3. Check if string starts with colon character (0x3A)\n4. If all validation passes, call processing function with string after colon\n5. Return result from processing function\n6. Return 0 if any validation check fails\n\nParameters:\nhContext1 - First context handle passed through to processing function\nhContext2 - Second context handle passed through to processing function\nlpszData - String data to validate for colon prefix\n\nReturns:\nProcessing result from FUN_68003580 if validation passes\n0 if validation fails (null pointer, empty string, or no colon prefix)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nColon character (0x3A) must be first character for processing\nString pointer is incremented by 1 to skip colon before processing\nEmpty strings (null terminator at first position) treated as validation failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3A (58) - ASCII colon character used as required prefix\n0x00 (0) - Return value for all validation failure cases",
