      "api_count": 0,
      "api_calls": [],
      "instructions": ["0x3100|SUB|ESP, 0x404", "0x3106|PUSH|EBP", "0x3107|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x40c]", "0x310E|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x3110|PUSH|EDI", "0x3111|JNZ|0x6800311e", "0x3113|POP|EDI", "0x3114|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x3116|POP|EBP", "0x3117|ADD|ESP, 0x404", "0x311D|RET|", "0x311E|PUSH|0x6800ef64", "0x3123|PUSH|EBP", "0x3124|CALL|dword ptr [0x6800b174]", "0x312A|MOV|EDI, EAX"],
      "comment": "Loads patch configuration entries from a script file into the global patch array\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input script file path parameter is not NULL\n2. Open script file in read mode using global file mode string\n3. Log error and return 0 if file cannot be opened\n4. Initialize patch counting variables and clear existing cleanup handle\n5. Free any existing cleanup resources if handle is allocated\n6. Read file line by line using 1024-byte buffer until EOF\n7. Calculate string length using SCASB.REPNE for each line\n8. Strip trailing CR (0x0D) and LF (0x0A) characters from line end\n9. Null-terminate the cleaned line string\n10. Resize patch array if current count exceeds allocated entries (grow by 10)\n11. Parse line into PatchEntry structure using FUN_680032e0\n12. If parse successful, increment patch count and advance array offset by 44 bytes\n13. Continue reading lines until EOF reached\n14. Close file handle and mark end of patch array with sentinel value 0xFFFFFFFF\n15. Log completion message with patch count and filename\n16. Return 1 for success\n\nParameters:\nlpszScriptFilePath - Absolute or relative path to script configuration file\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success, patches loaded into global array\n0 - Failure, null parameter or file cannot be opened\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null parameter check returns 0 immediately\n- File open failure logs error message and returns 0\n- Empty lines or comment lines (starting with #) are skipped by parser\n- Array grows dynamically by 10 entries when space needed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x400 (1024) - Line buffer size for reading file content\n0x2C (44) - Size of PatchEntry structure in bytes  \n0x1B8 (440) - Realloc size calculation (10 entries * 44 bytes)\n0xFFFFFFFF - Sentinel value marking end of patch array\n0x0D (13) - Carriage Return character for line ending\n0x0A (10) - Line Feed character for line ending\n\nStructure Layout:\nPatchEntry (44 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type    | Description\n0x00   | 4    | szPatchName     | char*   | Name/identifier for patch\n0x04   | 4    | dwBaseAddress   | uint    | Target memory address\n0x08   | 4    | dwOriginalDataSize | uint | Size of original data\n0x0C   | 4    | pbOriginalData  | byte*   | Pointer to original bytes\n0x10   | 4    | dwNewDataSize   | uint    | Size of replacement data\n0x14   | 4    | pbNewData       | byte*   | Pointer to new bytes\n0x18   | 4    | dwFlags         | uint    | Patch configuration flags\n0x1C   | 4    | dwReserved1     | uint    | Reserved field\n0x20   | 4    | dwReserved2     | uint    | Reserved field\n0x24   | 4    | szComment       | char*   | Optional comment string\n0x28   | 4    | dwReserved3     | uint    | Reserved field\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid file path logged with g_pfnLogHandler callback\n- Realloc failure would cause access violation (no error checking)\n- Parse failure for individual lines skips entry but continues processing\n- EOF condition terminates loop normally",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
