      "comment": "Parse configuration structure from command line arguments\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - check pConfig and pArgc not NULL\n2. Check command line not starting with '#' (comment marker)  \n3. Parse command line arguments into string array using ParseCommandLineArguments\n4. Validate minimum 4 arguments required for basic configuration\n5. Parse second argument as numeric value using strtoul with base detection\n6. Check for optional parameter suffix after numeric value (separated by delimiter)\n7. Duplicate first argument as configuration name string\n8. Parse third argument as hex buffer using ParseHexStringToBuffer  \n9. Parse fourth argument as second hex buffer using ParseHexStringToBuffer\n10. Store parsed values into CommandConfig structure fields\n11. Parse optional fifth argument as hex parameter if present\n12. Initialize reserved fields to zero and store optional parameter\n13. Clean up allocated memory and return success/failure status\n\nParameters:\npConfig - Pointer to CommandConfig structure to populate with parsed values\npArgc - Pointer to argument count, modified during parsing\n\nReturns:  \n1 - Successfully parsed configuration from command line\n0 - Parsing failed due to invalid parameters, insufficient arguments, or parse errors\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type     Description\n0x00    4     lpszName            char*    Configuration name string (duplicated)\n0x04    4     dwValue             uint     Parsed numeric value from second argument  \n0x08    4     nBufferSize1        int      Size of first parsed hex buffer\n0x0C    4     pBuffer1            void*    First hex buffer data\n0x10    4     nBufferSize2        int      Size of second parsed hex buffer\n0x14    4     pBuffer2            void*    Second hex buffer data\n0x18    4     dwHexParam          uint     Optional hex parameter (default 0)\n0x1C    4     dwReserved1         uint     Reserved field (set to 0)\n0x20    4     dwReserved2         uint     Reserved field (set to 0)  \n0x24    4     lpszOptionalParam   char*    Optional parameter string or NULL\n0x28    4     dwReserved3         uint     Reserved field (set to 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if pConfig or pArgc is NULL\n- Returns 0 if command line starts with '#' character (comment line)\n- Returns 0 if ParseCommandLineArguments fails or returns NULL\n- Returns 0 if fewer than 4 arguments provided\n- lpszOptionalParam set to NULL if no delimiter found in numeric argument\n- dwHexParam defaults to 0 if fifth argument not provided\n- Uses base-0 parsing for numeric value (detects hex/decimal automatically)\n- Uses base-16 parsing for optional hex parameter",
