      "comment": "Search for a command entry in the global command table by name.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize table pointer to g_pCommandTable (global command table)\n2. Check if command table is valid (not NULL)\n3. Begin linear search through command table entries\n4. For each entry: call _stricmp to compare entry command string with search parameter\n5. If comparison returns 0 (match found), return pointer to current entry\n6. Advance to next entry by adding 12 bytes (sizeof(CommandEntry))\n7. Continue loop while next entry's command string is not NULL\n8. If no match found after scanning entire table, return NULL\n\nParameters:\nlpszCommand (char *): Case-insensitive command string to search for in table\n\nReturns:\nCommandEntry *: Pointer to matching command table entry on success\nNULL: Command not found in table or table is empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns NULL if g_pCommandTable is NULL (uninitialized)\n- Returns NULL if lpszCommand is NULL (handled by _stricmp)\n- Table must be NULL-terminated (final entry has lpszCommand = NULL)\n\nStructure Layout:\nCommandEntry (12 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type     | Description\n0x00   | 4    | lpszCommand     | char *   | Pointer to command name string\n0x04   | 4    | lpszDescription | char *   | Pointer to command help text  \n0x08   | 4    | pHandler        | void *   | Pointer to command handler function\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0C (12): Size of CommandEntry structure in bytes",
