      "comment": "Validates system packet structure and calls appropriate validator function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if packet size is zero, return 0 (invalid) if empty\n2. Extract packet type from offset 4, adjust by subtracting 0x99 (0x67 complement)\n3. Validate packet type is within valid range (0-9)\n4. Look up expected packet size in g_adwSystemPacketSizeTable[packetType]\n5. Validate actual packet size matches expected size (if size table entry exists)\n6. Call packet-specific validator function from g_apfnSystemPacketValidators[packetType]\n7. Handle validator return codes: 3 indicates critical error, trigger error handler\n8. Log error for invalid packet types or validation failures\n\nParameters:\npPacket (SystemPacket*): Pointer to system packet structure to validate\nnPacketSize (int): Size of packet in bytes\n\nReturns:\n1: Packet validation successful\n0: Packet validation failed (size mismatch, invalid type, validator failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Packet type >= 10: Logs \"unknown sys packet type\" error\n- Size mismatch: Logs \"bad sys packet size\" error with type and sizes\n- Validator return code 3: Triggers special error handler FUN_68007060\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x99 (153): Packet type adjustment offset (complement of 0x67)\n0x67 (103): Base packet type value for adjustment calculation\n10: Maximum valid packet type index\n3: Critical error code from validator functions\n-1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Skip size validation marker in size table\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwHeader   | uint | Packet header/identifier\n0x4    | 1    | byType     | byte | Packet type code (adjusted by +0x99)",
