      "comment": "Processes and validates client packet data, performing integrity checks and updating client state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global connection state at ram0x68010ef0+0x3c, return 3 if inactive\n2. Get client context handle via g_pfnGetClientContext function pointer \n3. Get client info handle via g_pfnGetClientInfo function pointer\n4. Retrieve ClientInfo structure pointer from handle+0x68 offset\n5. Validate ClientInfo integrity: check null pointer, self-reference consistency, client ID match\n6. If packet type at +1 is 0x01 (authenticated packet):\n   - Calculate checksum using XOR of packet+6 with (context+0x28 * 3)  \n   - Verify checksum against ~packet+10 XOR calculated value compared to ram0x68010ef0+0x40\n   - Call IsActiveConnection with transformed connection ID parameter\n   - Set client flags +0x8 |= 0x04 if connection active, else timeout = 1000ms\n7. If packet type not 0x01 or checksum invalid, set timeout = 1000ms\n8. Update client timestamp with GetTickCount result\n9. Call g_pfnFinalizeEntity cleanup function\n10. Return status code 2 (processed)\n\nParameters:\nnClientId (ECX) - Client identifier for validation against ClientInfo\npbPacketData (EDX) - Pointer to packet buffer for processing\nIMPLICIT: Uses global context state, function pointers, and ClientInfo structure\n\nReturns:\n3 - Connection inactive (early exit)\n2 - Packet processed successfully or with validation errors\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers: 0x01 = authenticated packet type, 1000 = timeout value in milliseconds\nChecksum validation uses triple multiplication factor from context+0x28\nConnection ID transformation subtracts triple factor and XORs with base checksum\n\nError Handling:\nNull ClientInfo pointer - logs error and returns 2\nClientInfo self-reference mismatch - logs pointer corruption and returns 2  \nClient ID mismatch - logs ID validation failure and returns 2\nInvalid checksum or packet type - sets 1000ms timeout, continues processing\n\nStructure Layout:\nClientInfo (32 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | pSelf         | ptr  | Self-reference integrity check\n0x04   | 4    | dwClientId    | uint | Client identifier \n0x08   | 4    | dwFlags       | uint | Status flags (bit 2 = active connection)\n0x0C   | 4    | dwReserved    | uint | Reserved field\n0x10   | 4    | dwTimeout     | uint | Timeout value in milliseconds\n0x14   | 4    | dwReserved2   | uint | Reserved field  \n0x18   | 4    | dwReserved3   | uint | Reserved field\n0x1C   | 4    | dwTimestamp   | uint | Last activity timestamp\n\nNote: Function uses SSA temporary variables created by decompiler (piVar1, iVar3, etc.)\nAll local variables are compiler-generated register temporaries, not user-allocated storage.",
