      "comment": "Checks if a connection ID exists in the active connections list\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if any active connections exist (dwActiveConnectionCount > 0)\n2. Initialize loop index to 0 and pointer to connection array start\n3. Loop through active connections array:\n   a. Verify index is within bounds (< 16 maximum connections)\n   b. Compare current connection ID with search target\n   c. Return true if match found\n   d. Increment index and advance array pointer\n   e. Continue while index < active connection count\n4. Return false if no match found or no active connections\n\nParameters:\n   nConnectionId - Connection ID to search for in active list\n\nReturns:\n   true - Connection ID found in active connections array\n   false - Connection ID not found or no active connections exist\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Returns false immediately if no active connections (count = 0)\n   - Enforces maximum of 16 connections (0x10) with bounds check\n   - Early termination on bounds violation prevents buffer overflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n   0x44 - Offset to dwActiveConnectionCount in GameServerState\n   0x48 - Offset to adActiveConnections array in GameServerState  \n   0x10 (16) - Maximum allowed active connections\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name              | Type     | Description\n-------|------|-------------------------|----------|---------------------------\n0x44   | 4    | dwActiveConnectionCount | uint     | Count of active connections\n0x48   | 64   | adActiveConnections     | int[16]  | Array of connection IDs",
