      "instructions": ["0x3B40|PUSH|EBP", "0x3B41|PUSH|ESI", "0x3B42|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x3B44|PUSH|ESI", "0x3B45|CALL|0x68003c50", "0x3B4A|ADD|ESP, 0x4", "0x3B4D|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x3B4F|CALL|dword ptr [0x68014638]", "0x3B55|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x3B57|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x3B59|JZ|0x68003c46", "0x3B5F|PUSH|EBX", "0x3B60|MOV|EDX, ESI", "0x3B62|MOV|ECX, EBP", "0x3B64|CALL|dword ptr [0x68014610]"],
      "comment": "Validates client connection and processes client data if all validation checks pass.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call preprocessing function FUN_68003c50 with client ID\n2. Retrieve game state object through DAT_68014638 function pointer\n3. Return 0 immediately if game state is null (early exit)\n4. Retrieve client data object through DAT_68014610 function pointer  \n5. If client data is null, proceed to cleanup and return 0\n6. Extract ClientInfo structure pointer from client data at offset 0x68\n7. Validate ClientInfo pointer is not null, log error and exit if null\n8. Validate ClientInfo self-reference consistency (pointer[0] == pointer)\n9. Validate ClientInfo client ID matches input parameter (pointer[1] == dwClientId)\n10. Retrieve game entry using game ID from game state at offset 0x28\n11. If game entry exists and flag 0x8 is set, call FormatStringToCallback\n12. Check global condition at ram0x68010ef0+0x3c and client flags at offset 0x8\n13. If conditions met, set client timeout value to 1000 at offset 0x10\n14. Call cleanup function through g_pfnFinalizeEntity and return 0\n\nParameters:\ndwClientId (uint): Client identifier to validate and process\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 0 (success/completion indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game state null: Early return without processing\n- Client data null: Skip to cleanup, no error logged\n- ClientInfo null: Logs \"got NULL ClientInfo on Client\" error\n- Pointer mismatch: Logs \"ClientInfo ptr mismatch\" with pointer values  \n- ID mismatch: Logs \"ClientInfo id mismatch\" with expected vs actual IDs\n- All validation failures trigger immediate cleanup and return\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x68 - Offset to ClientInfo pointer in client data structure\n0x28 - Offset to game ID in game state structure  \n0x8 - Flag bit for game entry processing permission\n0x8 - Flag bit at ClientInfo+0x8 for client state validation\n0x10 - Offset for timeout value in ClientInfo structure\n1000 (0x3E8) - Timeout value in milliseconds for client processing\n0x3c - Offset in global structure for final condition check\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL game state: Silent early return\n- NULL client data: Silent cleanup without error\n- NULL ClientInfo: Debug log with client ID, then cleanup  \n- Pointer consistency fail: Debug log with both pointer values, then cleanup\n- Client ID mismatch: Debug log with expected and actual IDs, then cleanup\n- All error paths call g_pfnFinalizeEntity before returning\n\nStructure Layout:\nClientInfo Structure (32 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type      | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-----------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | pSelf         | ClientInfo*| Self-reference pointer for validation\n0x04   | 4    | dwClientId    | uint      | Client identifier for matching\n0x08   | 1    | bFlags        | byte      | Client state flags (bit 2 = timeout disable)\n0x10   | 4    | dwTimeout     | uint      | Client timeout value in milliseconds",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
