      "instructions": ["0x3C50|MOV|EAX, [0x680131d4]", "0x3C55|SUB|ESP, 0x18", "0x3C58|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x3C5A|PUSH|EBX", "0x3C5B|PUSH|EBP", "0x3C5C|JZ|0x68003da0", "0x3C62|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x24]", "0x3C66|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0x3C68|CALL|dword ptr [0x68014638]", "0x3C6E|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x3C70|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x3C72|JZ|0x68003da0", "0x3C78|PUSH|EDI", "0x3C79|MOV|EDX, EBX", "0x3C7B|MOV|ECX, EBP"],
      "comment": "Validates client anti-cheat status and updates cryptographic authentication data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if anti-cheat system is enabled (g_dwAntiCheatStatus != 0)\n2. Get client context using g_pfnGetClientContext callback\n3. Retrieve client info structure using g_pfnGetClientInfo callback  \n4. Extract ClientInfo pointer from context at offset 0x68\n5. Validate ClientInfo structure integrity:\n   - Check for NULL pointer (exit with error log if NULL)\n   - Verify self-reference pointer at offset 0x0 matches structure address\n   - Confirm client ID at offset 0x4 matches input parameter\n6. Reset anti-cheat counter if it exceeds g_dwAntiCheatCount limit\n7. Generate cryptographic data using FUN_68003db0 with current counter\n8. Create crypto packet header with magic byte 0xad\n9. Apply bit transformation to client ID and temp value:\n   - Extract high/low 16-bit words, XOR them, recombine with low word\n10. Store transformed crypto values in ClientInfo at offsets 0x24 and 0x28\n11. Notify system using g_pfnFormatCallback with parameter 9\n12. Clean up context using g_pfnFinalizeEntity\n\nParameters:\ndwClientId - Client identifier to validate and process\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, logs errors on validation failures\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Anti-cheat disabled: Function returns immediately without processing\n- NULL context/ClientInfo: Logs error and exits gracefully\n- Structure integrity failures: Logs specific mismatch and exits\n- Counter overflow: Resets to 0 when exceeding g_dwAntiCheatCount\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x68 - Offset to ClientInfo pointer in client context structure\n0x0 - Self-reference pointer offset in ClientInfo  \n0x4 - Client ID offset in ClientInfo\n0x24 - First crypto data storage offset in ClientInfo (piVar1[9])\n0x28 - Second crypto data storage offset in ClientInfo (piVar1[10])\n0x30 - Anti-cheat counter offset in ClientInfo (piVar1[0xc]) \n0xad - Magic byte header for crypto packet\n0xffff - 16-bit mask for word extraction in bit transformation\n0x10 - Right shift count for extracting high word\n9 - Parameter passed to g_pfnFormatCallback\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL ClientInfo → InitializeDebugLogAndWrite with \"got NULL ClientInfo\"\n- Self-reference mismatch → Log \"ClientInfo ptr mismatch\" with pointers\n- Client ID mismatch → Log \"ClientInfo id mismatch\" with IDs  \n- All errors call g_pfnFinalizeEntity for cleanup before return\n\nStructure Layout:\nClientInfo structure (32 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x0    | 4    | pSelf      | ClientInfo* | Self-reference pointer for integrity\n0x4    | 4    | dwId       | uint | Client identifier  \n...    | ...  | ...        | ... | ... (other fields not accessed)\n0x24   | 4    | dwCrypto1  | uint | First transformed crypto value\n0x28   | 4    | dwCrypto2  | uint | Second transformed crypto value  \n0x30   | 4    | dwCounter  | uint | Anti-cheat operation counter",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
