      "comment": "Retrieves two pairs of anti-cheat addresses from global table with random selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate table index and clamp to zero if out of bounds\n2. Extract first address pair from table at specified index\n3. Store first address and size to output parameters\n4. Generate random offset within valid range (1 to count-1)\n5. Calculate second table index by adding random offset\n6. Apply modulo if second index exceeds table bounds\n7. Extract second address pair from table at calculated index\n8. Store second address and size to output parameters\n\nParameters:\ndwTableIndex - Index into anti-cheat address table (0-based)\npFirstAddress - Pointer to receive first anti-cheat address\npSecondAddress - Pointer to receive second anti-cheat address (randomized)\npFirstSize - Pointer to receive first anti-cheat memory size\npSecondSize - Pointer to receive second anti-cheat memory size (randomized)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, results provided through output parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIndex validation: dwTableIndex >= g_dwAntiCheatCount -> clamped to 0\nBounds checking: Second index >= g_dwAntiCheatCount -> wrapped with modulo\nRandom range: Always generates offset 1 to (count-1) to ensure different pairs\n\nStructure Layout:\ng_adAntiCheatAddresses table layout (8-byte stride):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | address    | uint | Memory address to protect\n0x04   | 4    | size       | uint | Size of protected region\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x02 (decimal 2) - Stride multiplier for address pair access\n0x01 (decimal 1) - Minimum random offset to ensure different selection",
