      "instructions": ["0x3E30|PUSH|ECX", "0x3E31|PUSH|EBX", "0x3E32|PUSH|EDI", "0x3E33|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x3E35|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x3E37|PUSH|EDI", "0x3E38|CALL|0x68003c50", "0x3E3D|MOV|EAX, [0x68010ef0]", "0x3E42|ADD|ESP, 0x4", "0x3E45|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x3c]", "0x3E48|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x3E4A|JNZ|0x68003e54", "0x3E4C|POP|EDI", "0x3E4D|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x3E4F|POP|EBX"],
      "comment": "Validates client anti-cheat information and handles version compatibility checks\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ValidateClientInfoAndUpdateCrypto to verify basic client credentials\n2. Check if the game server is active by reading configuration from ram0x68010ef0+0x3c\n3. Retrieve client context via g_pfnGetClientContext function pointer\n4. Retrieve client info object via g_pfnGetClientInfo function pointer\n5. Extract ClientInfo structure pointer from offset 0x68 of client object\n6. Validate ClientInfo structure integrity with three checks:\n   - NULL pointer check (offset 0x0)\n   - Self-reference validation (offset 0x0 must point to itself)\n   - Client ID match validation (offset 0x4 must match dwClientId parameter)\n7. Extract version/type data from packet at offset 0x1\n8. Check anti-cheat flag status at ClientInfo offset 0x8, bit 2 (0x02)\n9. If anti-cheat already enabled, perform connection validation:\n   - Calculate crypto hash using ~dwVersion * dwVersion XOR context+0x28 XOR packet+0x5\n   - Call IsActiveConnection with computed hash\n   - Set timeout error (1000) if connection inactive\n   - Clear packet validation field at offset 0x5\n10. If anti-cheat not enabled, set flag bit 2 (0x02) in ClientInfo offset 0x8\n11. Handle validation status from packet offset 0x5:\n    - Value -1: Check version compatibility, set update message if outdated, return success (1)\n    - Value 0: Set update message and timeout error\n    - Other values: Set timeout error\n12. Call g_pfnFinalizeEntity cleanup function before returning\n\nParameters:\ndwClientId - Client identifier for validation\npPacketData - Pointer to anti-cheat packet data containing version and validation status\n\nReturns:\n1 - Anti-cheat validation successful (version check passed)\n0 - Validation failed (various error conditions)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nServer inactive (config value 0) - Return 0 immediately\nNULL ClientInfo pointer - Log error and return 0\nClientInfo self-reference mismatch - Log error and return 0  \nClient ID mismatch - Log error and return 0\nAnti-cheat already active - Perform connection check and return 0\nOutdated client version - Set update message and appropriate return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x02 - Anti-cheat enabled flag bit in ClientInfo structure\n0x68 - Offset to ClientInfo pointer in client object\n1000 - Timeout/error code value (0x3E8)\n-1 - Special validation status indicating version check mode\n0x3c - Offset to server active flag in global configuration\n\nError Handling:\nAll validation failures log detailed error messages via InitializeDebugLogAndWrite\nCleanup via g_pfnFinalizeEntity called before error returns\nTimeout errors set to 1000 in ClientInfo structure offset 0x10\nUpdate message pointer stored at ClientInfo offset 0xC\n\nStructure Layout:\nClientInfo Structure (32 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type        Description\n0x00    4     pSelfRef        ClientInfo* Self-reference pointer for validation\n0x04    4     dwClientId      uint        Client identifier\n0x08    4     dwFlags         uint        Status flags (bit 2 = anti-cheat enabled)\n0x0C    4     pMessage        char*       Error/update message pointer\n0x10    4     dwTimeoutCode   uint        Timeout/error code value\n\nAntiCheatPacket Structure (9 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type        Description  \n0x00    1     byHeader        byte        Packet header/type\n0x01    4     dwVersion       uint        Client version or type identifier\n0x05    4     nValidation     int         Validation status (-1, 0, or other)\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit 2 (0x02) - Anti-cheat system enabled flag\nTest: (dwFlags & 2U) != 0",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
