      "instructions": ["0x4030|SUB|ESP, 0x98", "0x4036|PUSH|EDI", "0x4037|MOV|ECX, 0x99", "0x403C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x403E|MOV|EDI, 0x68010f48", "0x4043|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0x4045|PUSH|0x68011168", "0x404A|CALL|dword ptr [0x6800b064]", "0x4050|PUSH|0x6801118c", "0x4055|CALL|dword ptr [0x6800b060]", "0x405B|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x8]", "0x405F|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], 0x94", "0x4067|PUSH|EAX", "0x4068|CALL|dword ptr [0x6800b050]", "0x406E|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Initializes comprehensive system information structure with OS details, hardware info, and user context\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-initialize 613-byte SystemInfoBlock structure (0x99 dwords)\n2. Collect system information via GetSystemInfo() and GlobalMemoryStatus()\n3. Retrieve OS version details via GetVersionExA()\n4. Set Windows NT flag if platform ID equals 2 (VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT)\n5. Get computer information via custom function FUN_68004420()\n6. Retrieve current user name via GetUserNameA() with 257-byte buffer\n7. Retrieve computer name via GetComputerNameA() with 16-byte buffer\n8. Get process and system affinity masks via GetProcessAffinityMask()\n9. Determine processor architecture from SYSTEM_INFO.wProcessorArchitecture\n10. Set CPU identification strings based on processor type:\n    - 0x00: Intel x86 based on SYSTEM_INFO.wProcessorLevel (0x182=i386, 0x1e6=i486, 0x24a=Pentium)\n    - 0x01: MIPS processor (R4000 series)\n    - 0x02: Alpha processor (21064/21164/21264 variants)  \n    - 0x03: PowerPC processor\n    - Default: Generic Intel x86\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nSystemInfoBlock * - Pointer to populated system information structure at 0x68010f48\n                   Contains OS version, hardware details, user context, and CPU identification\n\nSpecial Cases:\nError conditions logged via global function pointer g_pfnLogHandler:\n- GetVersionExA() failure: \"Error Getting Version Info\"\n- GetUserNameA() failure: \"Error Getting User Name\"  \n- GetComputerNameA() failure: \"Error Getting Computer Name\"\n- GetProcessAffinityMask() failure: \"Error Getting Process Affinity Mask\"\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x99 (153) - Number of dwords to zero-initialize (613 total bytes)\n0x94 (148) - Size of OSVERSIONINFOA structure\n0x101 (257) - Buffer size for user name (including null terminator)\n0x10 (16) - Buffer size for computer name\n0x02 - VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT platform identifier\n0x182 (386) - Intel i386 processor level identifier\n0x1e6 (486) - Intel i486 processor level identifier  \n0x24a (586) - Intel Pentium processor level identifier\n\nStructure Layout:\nSystemInfoBlock at 0x68010f48 (613 bytes total):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type        Description\n0x00    4     dwIsWindowsNT          uint        Windows NT flag (0=Win9x, 1=WinNT)\n0x04    4     dwProcessAffinityMask  uint        Process affinity mask from API\n0x08    16    szComputerName         char[16]    Computer name from GetComputerNameA\n0x18    257   szUserName             char[257]   User name from GetUserNameA  \n0x119   64    cpuInfo                byte[64]    CPU identification strings\n0x159   36    systemInfo             byte[36]    SYSTEM_INFO structure from GetSystemInfo\n0x17D   32    memoryStatus           byte[32]    MEMORYSTATUS from GlobalMemoryStatus\n0x19D   200   reserved               byte[200]   Reserved/padding space",
