      "instructions": ["0x42C0|PUSH|EBP", "0x42C1|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x42C3|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0x42C6|PUSH|EBX", "0x42C7|MOV|EAX, 0x0", "0x42CC|CPUID|", "0x42CE|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x1c], EBX", "0x42D1|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x18], EDX", "0x42D4|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x14], ECX", "0x42D7|MOV|byte ptr [EBP + -0x10], 0x0", "0x42DB|MOV|EAX, 0x1", "0x42E0|CPUID|", "0x42E2|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x8], EAX", "0x42E5|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EBX", "0x42E8|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0xc], EDX"],
      "comment": "Formats CPU identification information into a human-readable string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute CPUID instruction with EAX=0 to get vendor identification string\n2. Store vendor string components (EBX, EDX, ECX) in local variables dwVendorId1-3\n3. Add null terminator (0x00) to complete vendor string\n4. Execute CPUID instruction with EAX=1 to get version information\n5. Store version/feature information (EAX, EBX, EDX) in local variables\n6. Extract CPU type field from bits 12-15 of version info (SAR 0xc, AND 0xf)\n7. Extract family field from bits 8-11 of version info (SAR 0x8, AND 0xf)  \n8. Extract model field from bits 4-7 of version info (SAR 0x4, AND 0xf)\n9. Extract stepping field from bits 0-3 of version info (AND 0xf)\n10. Extract brand index from bits 0-7 of brand info (AND 0xff)\n11. Format all extracted information using sprintf with format string\n12. Return 1 to indicate successful completion\n\nParameters:\nlpszOutputBuffer: char * - Target buffer to receive formatted CPU information string\n\nReturns:\n1: Always indicates successful completion of CPU information formatting\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x00: EAX value for CPUID vendor identification\n0x01: EAX value for CPUID version/feature information\n0xf: Mask for 4-bit fields (type, family, model, stepping)\n0xff: Mask for 8-bit brand index field\n0xc: Right shift count for type field (bits 12-15)\n0x8: Right shift count for family field (bits 8-11) \n0x4: Right shift count for model field (bits 4-7)\n\nError Handling:\nFunction assumes CPUID instruction is available and supported by processor\nNo validation performed on output buffer size or validity\nNo error conditions detected - always returns success",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1"]
    },
