      "comment": "Measures the CPU frequency using RDTSC instruction and high-resolution performance counters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query performance counter frequency using QueryPerformanceFrequency\n2. Get current thread handle and save original priority\n3. Set thread priority to THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL (0xf) for accurate timing\n4. Wait for stable timing conditions (minimum 16ms gap between tick measurements) \n5. Take RDTSC timestamp and performance counter baseline measurements\n6. Wait for sufficient time gap (at least 16 ticks) for accurate measurement\n7. Take final RDTSC timestamp and performance counter measurements\n8. Restore original thread priority\n9. Calculate CPU frequency: (RDTSC_delta * perf_freq) / perf_counter_delta\n10. Return calculated frequency in Hz\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint: CPU frequency in Hz on success\nuint: 0 if QueryPerformanceFrequency fails, thread priority invalid, or priority change fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if high-resolution performance counter not available\n- Returns 0 if original thread priority is THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN (0x7fffffff)\n- Returns 0 if unable to set thread to time-critical priority\n- Loops until minimum 16 tick gap achieved for stable measurement\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7fffffff (2147483647): THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN constant\n0xf (15): THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL for accurate timing\n0x10 (16): Minimum tick count difference for stable measurement",
