      "comment": "Converts ASCII character to hexadecimal digit value (0-15).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract lower 8 bits from input to get character value\n2. Call tolower() to convert character to lowercase  \n3. Compare against 0x41 ('A') to determine digit type\n4. If character < 'A', subtract 0x30 to convert '0'-'9' to 0-9\n5. If character >= 'A', add 0xA9 (-0x57) to convert 'a'-'f' to 10-15\n6. Return hexadecimal digit value as byte\n\nParameters:\ndwInput - uint: ASCII character value in lower 8 bits (accepts 0-255)\n\nReturns:\nbyte: Hexadecimal digit value (0-15 for valid hex chars, undefined for invalid)\nSuccess: 0-15 for valid hex digits '0'-'9' and 'a'-'f'/'A'-'F'\nInvalid input: Returns undefined arithmetic result for non-hex characters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCharacters '0'-'9': Converted to values 0-9 via subtraction (char - 0x30)\nCharacters 'A'-'F': Converted via tolower() then arithmetic (char + 0xA9)\nInvalid characters: No validation, returns arithmetic result which may be invalid\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFF - Mask to extract lower 8 bits from input parameter\n0x30 - ASCII value of '0', subtracted to convert digit chars to numeric values\n0x41 - ASCII value of 'A', comparison threshold for letter vs digit\n0xA9 - Adjustment constant (-0x57) to convert 'a'-'f' to values 10-15",
