      "comment": "Processes C-style escape sequences in input string and converts them to their actual byte values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output index and input index to 0\n2. Loop through input string while output index < maximum output length\n3. Read current character from input string at current input index\n4. If character is null terminator (0x00), return current output index (end of string)\n5. If character is backslash (0x5C), process escape sequence:\n   a. Read next character after backslash\n   b. If next character is null, return current output index (incomplete escape)\n   c. If next character is backslash, write literal backslash (0x5C) to output\n   d. If next character is 'x', process hexadecimal escape sequence:\n      - Check if next two characters are valid hex digits using _isctype with 0x80 mask\n      - If first character not hex digit, write literal 'x' (0x78) to output\n      - If second character not hex digit, convert first hex digit only\n      - If both hex digits valid, convert to byte value (high nibble << 4 + low nibble)\n   e. If next character is standard escape character, convert to control code:\n      - 'n' -> newline (0x0A)\n      - 'r' -> carriage return (0x0D)  \n      - 'a' -> bell/alert (0x07)\n      - 't' -> horizontal tab (0x09)\n      - 'b' -> backspace (0x08)\n      - 'f' -> form feed (0x0C)\n      - 'v' -> vertical tab (0x0B)\n      - Any other character -> write literal character to output\n6. If character is not backslash, write character directly to output\n7. Increment output index and input index, continue loop\n8. Return final output index (number of bytes written)\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (int): Pointer to null-terminated input string containing escape sequences\nparam_2 (int): Pointer to output buffer where processed bytes will be written  \nparam_3 (uint): Maximum number of bytes to write to output buffer (prevents overflow)\n\nReturns:\nNumber of bytes successfully written to output buffer (0 to param_3)\nReturns early if null terminator encountered or incomplete escape sequence found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Incomplete escape sequences (backslash at end of string) terminate processing\n- Invalid hex digits in \\x sequences result in literal character output\n- Output buffer overflow protection via param_3 limit\n- Single hex digit after \\x processes one character and writes literal byte\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5C (92) - Backslash character for escape sequence detection\n0x78 (120) - Character 'x' for hexadecimal escape sequences  \n0x0A (10) - Newline character for \n escape\n0x0D (13) - Carriage return character for \\r escape\n0x07 (7) - Bell/alert character for \\a escape\n0x09 (9) - Horizontal tab character for \\t escape\n0x08 (8) - Backspace character for \\b escape\n0x0C (12) - Form feed character for \\f escape\n0x0B (11) - Vertical tab character for \\v escape\n0x80 - _isctype mask for hexadecimal digit classification\n0x10 (16) - Left shift value for hex high nibble conversion\n\nError Handling:\n- Null terminator detection prevents buffer overrun on input\n- Output buffer length checking prevents buffer overrun on output\n- Invalid hex digit handling falls back to literal character output\n- Incomplete escape sequences terminate processing gracefully",
