      "comment": "Splits an input string into tokens using specified delimiter characters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (lpszInput and lpszDelimiters not NULL)\n2. Calculate input string length using SCASB.REPNE instruction\n3. Allocate temporary token buffer with malloc(stringLength)\n4. Allocate initial token pointer array (32 entries, 128 bytes)\n5. Initialize state variables (token count=1, in_delimiter=true)\n6. Iterate through each character in input string:\n   a. Check if current character matches any delimiter\n   b. If delimiter found and not in_delimiter state, null-terminate token\n   c. If non-delimiter and in_delimiter state, start new token\n   d. Expand token array with realloc if capacity exceeded (grow by 32 entries)\n   e. Copy character to token buffer and advance pointer\n7. Allocate final result buffer combining token array and string data\n8. Copy token data to end of result buffer using MOVSD.REP\n9. Adjust token pointers to reference final buffer locations\n10. Copy token pointer array to beginning of result buffer\n11. Free temporary buffers (token buffer and original array)\n12. Set token count in output parameter if provided\n\nParameters:\nlpszInput - Source string to be tokenized (null-terminated)\nlpszDelimiters - String containing delimiter characters (null-terminated)  \npnTokenCount - Optional pointer to receive number of tokens found\n\nReturns:\nNon-NULL: Pointer to array of string pointers (null-terminated array)\nNULL: Memory allocation failed or invalid input parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty input string returns valid array with zero tokens\nMultiple consecutive delimiters treated as single separator\nLeading/trailing delimiters ignored\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 (32) - Initial token array capacity (entries)\n0x80 (128) - Initial token array size in bytes (32 * 4)\n0x4 (4) - Size of pointer on 32-bit system\n\nError Handling:\nReturns NULL on malloc/realloc failure\nFrees all allocated memory on error before returning\nParameter validation prevents null pointer dereference",
