      "comment": "Parses a command line string into an argv-style array of argument pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input command line string is not NULL\n2. Calculate string length using strlen-like loop with SCASB.REPNE instruction\n3. Allocate temporary buffer for processed argument strings using malloc\n4. Allocate initial argv pointer array with 32-pointer capacity (0x20)\n5. Parse arguments character by character in main processing loop:\n   - Skip leading whitespace characters (space 0x20, tab 0x09)\n   - Handle quoted strings (quote 0x22): process escape sequences (backslash 0x5C), copy until closing quote\n   - Handle unquoted strings: copy characters until whitespace or string termination\n   - Null-terminate each processed argument string\n   - Store string offset in argv array, expand array capacity when needed using realloc\n6. Allocate final result buffer combining argv array and string data\n7. Copy processed string data to end of result buffer using MOVSD.REP\n8. Update argv pointers to point into result buffer string area\n9. Set argv[argc] = NULL as standard array terminator\n10. Clean up temporary allocations and return argv array pointer\n\nParameters:\nlpszCommandLine - Input command line string to parse (char *)\npnArgCount - Optional output parameter for argument count, can be NULL (int *)\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Pointer to allocated argv array with embedded string data (char **)\n         Array is NULL-terminated, strings stored after array in same allocation\nFailure: NULL if input NULL, memory allocation fails, or realloc fails during parsing\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty or whitespace-only strings return NULL after validation\nQuoted strings support backslash escape sequences (\\\", \\\\)\nUnterminated quotes treated as extending to end of command line\nArray capacity grows by 32 pointers (0x20) when current capacity exceeded\nString buffer grows by 128 bytes (0x80) when capacity exceeded\nFinal allocation combines argv array and string data for single free() operation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 (32) - Initial capacity and increment size for argv pointer array\n0x80 (128) - Initial and increment size for temporary string buffer\n0x22 (34) - ASCII double quote character for string delimiters\n0x5C (92) - ASCII backslash character for escape sequence processing\n0x20 (32) - ASCII space character for whitespace detection\n0x09 (9) - ASCII tab character for whitespace detection\n\nError Handling:\nmalloc failure during initial allocations - returns NULL immediately\nrealloc failure during array expansion - frees all allocations and returns NULL\nAll temporary buffers freed on both success and failure paths\nMemory allocation combines argv array and strings for single deallocation",
