      "comment": "Concatenates an array of strings using the specified separator and returns allocated result string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (string array and separator must not be NULL)\n2. Allocate initial buffer of 0x400 (1024) bytes and initialize with empty string\n3. Initialize loop control variables and first-item flag\n4. For each string in array (controlled by nArraySize or until NULL terminator if nArraySize is 0):\n   a. Skip NULL entries in array and advance to next entry\n   b. Calculate required buffer size (current string + existing buffer + separator)\n   c. If buffer too small, reallocate with additional 0x400 bytes\n   d. If not first item, append separator string to buffer\n   e. Append current string to buffer using optimized memory copy\n   f. Set first-item flag to true after first string\n   g. Advance to next array element\n5. After processing all strings, reallocate buffer to exact string length\n6. Return final concatenated string or NULL on allocation failure\n\nParameters:\npplpszStringArray - Array of string pointers to concatenate\nlpszSeparator - Separator string to insert between array elements  \nnArraySize - Maximum number of elements to process (0 = process until NULL)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to allocated concatenated string with separators, or NULL on failure\nCaller responsible for freeing returned memory\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf nArraySize is 0, processes array until NULL pointer encountered\nIf allocation fails during realloc, frees existing buffer and returns NULL\nIf only final realloc fails, returns oversized buffer instead of NULL\nEmpty strings in array are preserved (separator still added)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x400 (1024) - Initial buffer size and expansion increment\n0xffffffff - String length calculation sentinel for strlen replacement",
