      "comment": "Validates PE file format and returns size of optional header.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate DOS header magic number (0x5A4D = \"MZ\")\n2. Extract PE header offset from DOS header (offset 0x3C)\n3. Validate PE header magic number (0x4550 = \"PE\")\n4. Extract and return optional header size from PE header (offset 0x50)\n\nParameters:\npDosHeader (IMAGE_DOS_HEADER *): Pointer to DOS header at start of PE file\n\nReturns:\nuint: Size of PE optional header in bytes (0 if validation fails)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if DOS magic number is not 0x5A4D\n- Returns 0 if PE magic number is not 0x4550\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x5A4D: DOS header signature (\"MZ\")\n- 0x4550: PE header signature (\"PE\") \n- 0x3C: Offset to PE header offset field in DOS header\n- 0x50: Offset to optional header size field in PE header\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid DOS header: Returns 0 immediately\n- Invalid PE header: Returns 0 immediately\n- No exceptions thrown, uses early return pattern\n\nStructure Layout:\nIMAGE_DOS_HEADER (partial):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type     Description\n0x00    2     e_magic       ushort   DOS signature (0x5A4D)\n0x3C    4     e_lfanew      uint     PE header offset\n\nPE Header (at DOS+e_lfanew, partial):\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type     Description  \n0x00    4     Signature     uint     PE signature (0x4550)\n0x50    2     SizeOfOptionalHeader  ushort  Optional header size",
