      "comment": "Parse hexadecimal string into binary buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (hexadecimal string and buffer length pointer)\n2. Calculate string length using manual strlen with SCASB.REPNE instruction\n3. Allocate buffer with malloc (string_length / 2 bytes for binary data)\n4. Initialize parsing state (character index = 0, buffer index = 0)\n5. Loop through input string character by character:\n   - Skip whitespace characters (space 0x20, tab 0x09)\n   - Extract 2-character hex pairs using strncpy\n   - Convert hex pair to unsigned long with strtoul base 16\n   - Store converted byte in output buffer\n   - Advance character index by 2, buffer index by 1\n6. Store final buffer length in output parameter\n7. Return allocated buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\n  lpszHexString (char *): Input hexadecimal string to parse\n  pnBufferLength (int *): Output pointer to store resulting buffer length\n\nReturns:\n  void *: Allocated buffer containing binary data, or NULL on error\n  - Success: Pointer to malloc'd buffer with converted binary data\n  - NULL: Invalid input parameters or malloc failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL input parameters return NULL immediately\n  - Whitespace (space, tab) characters are skipped during parsing\n  - String length calculation uses manual implementation for exact byte count\n  - Buffer allocated as (string_length / 2) to convert hex pairs to bytes\n  - Each hex pair (2 ASCII characters) becomes 1 binary byte\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20: ASCII space character (skipped during parsing)\n  0x09: ASCII tab character (skipped during parsing)  \n  0x10: Base 16 for strtoul hexadecimal conversion\n  0xffffffff: Initial value for manual string length calculation\n\nError Handling:\n  - NULL parameter validation prevents segmentation faults\n  - malloc failure returns NULL (caller responsible for checking)\n  - Invalid hex characters handled by strtoul (returns 0 for non-hex)\n  - No explicit bounds checking (relies on null-terminated string)",
