      "comment": "Performs secure memory copy with memory protection handling and instruction cache flushing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters: check null pointers and zero size\n2. Change destination memory protection to PAGE_READWRITE (0x04) \n3. Change source memory protection to PAGE_READWRITE (0x04)\n4. Perform optimized memory copy using DWORD and byte operations\n5. Restore source memory protection to original value  \n6. Restore destination memory protection to original value\n7. Flush instruction cache for destination memory range\n8. Return destination pointer on success or NULL on error\n\nParameters:\npDestination (void *): Target memory buffer for copy operation\npSource (void *): Source memory buffer to copy from\ndwSize (size_t): Number of bytes to copy between buffers\ndwDestProtection (DWORD): New protection flags for destination during copy\ndwSourceProtection (DWORD): New protection flags for source during copy \ndwOldDestProtection (DWORD): Original protection flags to restore for destination\ndwOldSourceProtection (DWORD): Original protection flags to restore for source\n\nReturns:\nvoid *: Destination pointer on successful completion\nNULL: Memory protection change failed or invalid parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\nReturns destination pointer unchanged if any parameter is NULL or size is zero\nLogs detailed error messages via g_pfnDebugLogger on VirtualProtect failures\nAttempts to restore destination protection even if source protection fails\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x04: PAGE_READWRITE protection flag for VirtualProtect calls\nError rollback ensures memory protection consistency on failure paths",
