      "comment": "Safely copies a null-terminated string from source to destination buffer with bounds checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (null pointer checks and buffer size validation)\n2. Return -1 immediately if source pointer is null or destination buffer is zero\n3. Initialize character copy counter to zero\n4. Calculate destination offset (destination buffer base minus source pointer)\n5. Enter copy loop if buffer size allows at least one character plus null terminator\n6. For each character: check for null terminator, copy character to destination, increment counters\n7. Continue until null terminator found or buffer limit reached (nBufferSize - 1)\n8. Null-terminate the destination string at the final position\n9. Return the number of characters successfully copied\n\nParameters:\nlpszDestBuffer - Destination buffer to receive the copied string\nlpszSource - Source null-terminated string to copy from  \nnBufferSize - Maximum size of destination buffer including null terminator\n\nReturns:\nNumber of characters copied (excluding null terminator) on success\n-1 if source pointer is null or destination buffer is zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf nBufferSize is 1 or less, only null terminator is written to destination\nIf source string is longer than buffer allows, truncates and null-terminates\nEmpty source string (immediate null) results in return value of 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFFFFFF (OR EAX, 0xffffffff) - Returns -1 for parameter validation failure\n-1 (param_3 + -1) - Buffer size minus one to reserve space for null terminator",
