      "comment": "Generates a random integer within the specified inclusive range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate the range size as (nMaxValue - nMinValue + 1)\n2. Check if range is zero (invalid range where max < min)\n3. If zero range, return 0 immediately (early exit)\n4. Call rand() to get a random number\n5. Use modulo operation to fit within range\n6. Add minimum value to shift result into target range\n\nParameters:\n- nMinValue: int - Minimum value of the range (inclusive)\n- nMaxValue: int - Maximum value of the range (inclusive)\n\nReturns:\n- int - Random integer between nMinValue and nMaxValue (inclusive)\n- Returns 0 if nMaxValue < nMinValue (invalid range)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Invalid range (nMaxValue < nMinValue): Returns 0\n- Single value range (nMaxValue == nMinValue): Returns that value\n- Full int range may cause modulo bias\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1: Constant added to calculate inclusive range size",
