      "comment": "Calculates a checksum of a buffer while excluding a 4-byte range from the calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input buffer pointer is not null, return 0 if null\n2. Initialize checksum accumulator to 0\n3. Initialize byte index counter to 0\n4. Loop through each byte in buffer:\n   a. Load current byte value from buffer[index]\n   b. Check if current index falls within exclusion range (offset to offset+3)\n   c. If within exclusion range, treat byte as 0; otherwise use actual byte value\n   d. Add byte value to checksum with overflow carry propagation\n   e. Shift checksum left by 1 bit and add carry from previous overflow\n   f. Increment index counter\n5. Continue loop until all bytes processed\n6. Return accumulated checksum value\n\nParameters:\npbBuffer - Pointer to byte buffer to checksum\ndwBufferSize - Size of buffer in bytes to process\ndwExclusionOffset - Starting offset of 4-byte range to exclude from checksum\n\nReturns:\nInteger checksum value calculated from buffer contents\nReturns 0 if pbBuffer is null\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf exclusion range extends beyond buffer end, only bytes within buffer bounds are excluded\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 (4) - Size of exclusion range in bytes\n0x0 - Byte value used to replace excluded bytes in checksum calculation",
