      "instructions": ["0x56F0|PUSH|ESI", "0x56F1|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x56F3|PUSH|EDI", "0x56F4|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x56F6|MOV|AX, word ptr [ESI + 0x28]", "0x56FA|PUSH|EAX", "0x56FB|CALL|0x680064e8", "0x5700|ADD|ESP, 0x4", "0x5703|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x5705|JZ|0x6800575c", "0x5707|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX]", "0x5709|TEST|CL, 0x8", "0x570C|JZ|0x6800575c", "0x570E|TEST|CL, 0x10", "0x5711|JNZ|0x6800575c"],
      "comment": "Conditionally handles messages by checking object flags and calling message handler function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve flag pointer from object+0x28 by calling FUN_680064e8 with ushort value\n2. Validate flag pointer is not null and check flag bits 0x08 and 0x10\n3. If flag 0x08 is set and flag 0x10 is clear, set flag 0x10 to mark as processed\n4. Check global handler enabled flag (g_dwMessageHandlerEnabled)\n5. If handler disabled, call with message code 0x14d (333) and return 0\n6. If handler enabled, set param5 to 0x14d and continue to normal call\n7. Call function pointer g_pfnMessageHandler with all parameters\n8. Return result from message handler call\n\nParameters:\npMessageObject (MessageObject*): Object pointer with ushort at offset 0x28\npContext (void*): Context object passed to message handler\ndwParam1 (uint): First message parameter passed to handler\ndwParam2 (uint): Second message parameter passed to handler\ndwParam3 (uint): Third message parameter passed to handler\ndwParam4 (uint): Fourth message parameter passed to handler\ndwParam5 (uint): Fifth message parameter, replaced with 0x14d in conditional path\ndwParam6 (uint): Sixth message parameter passed to handler\n\nReturns:\n0: When conditional handler is disabled and message processed with code 0x14d\nuint: Return value from message handler function call\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early if flag pointer lookup fails (null result)\n- Skips flag modification if flag 0x08 not set or flag 0x10 already set\n- Uses magic number 0x14d (333 decimal) for conditional message code\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x08 (8): Flag bit indicating object requires message processing\n0x10 (16): Flag bit indicating message has been processed for this object\n0x14d (333): Special message code used when handler is disabled\n0x28 (40): Offset in MessageObject structure containing ushort identifier\n\nFlag Bits:\n0x08: Message processing required flag\n0x10: Message processed flag (prevents duplicate processing)",
