      "instructions": ["0x5860|MOV|EAX, [0x680145ec]", "0x5865|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x680145e4]", "0x586B|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x68010ef0]", "0x5871|PUSH|EBX", "0x5872|PUSH|ESI", "0x5873|PUSH|EDI", "0x5874|LEA|EDI, [ECX + EAX*0x1]", "0x5877|MOV|ECX, 0x680134b8", "0x587C|LEA|ESI, [EDX + 0x8c]", "0x5882|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESI + -0x4]", "0x5885|MOV|EAX, 0x51eb851f", "0x588A|IMUL|EDX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x4]", "0x588E|MUL|EDX", "0x5890|MOV|EBX, EDX", "0x5892|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESI]"],
      "comment": "Calculates total statistics value with percentage-based modifiers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize accumulator with sum of two base statistics (g_nBaseStat2 + g_nBaseStat1)\n2. Set up pointers: g_aStatPairs for modifier values, g_pGameServerState[1].reserved1+4 for stat values\n3. Loop through StatPair array until reaching g_aStatPairsEnd:\n   a. Load current stat value from server state data\n   b. Load current modifier value from stat pairs array  \n   c. Calculate: (stat_value * modifier_value) / 100\n   d. Add result to running total\n   e. Advance both pointers by 8 bytes (next StatPair and corresponding server data)\n4. Return accumulated total\n\nParameters:\n   (none)\n\nReturns:\n   int: Total calculated statistic value with all percentage modifiers applied\n        Returns 0 if no base stats or modifiers are configured\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   Division by 100 uses optimized multiplication by reciprocal (0x51eb851f)\n   Loop processes exactly 3 StatPair entries based on array bounds\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n   0x51eb851f - Reciprocal multiplier for division by 100 (compiler optimization)\n   0x680134b8 - Start address of StatPair array (g_aStatPairs)\n   0x680134d0 - End address of StatPair array (g_aStatPairsEnd)\n   0x8 - Size of StatPair structure (2 int fields)\n\nStructure Layout:\n   StatPair:\n   Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n   0x00   | 4    | nValue1    | int  | First modifier value\n   0x04   | 4    | nValue2    | int  | Second modifier value\n\nError Handling:\n   No explicit error checking - relies on valid global state initialization",
