      "comment": "Process game entity with conditional callback execution based on flag validation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup Win32 structured exception handling frame\n2. Validate entity flags: check byEntityFlags < 3 to ensure valid entity type\n3. Call entity lookup function (FUN_680064e8) with entity type ID from offset 0x28\n4. Verify lookup returned valid pointer (non-NULL)\n5. Check global enable flag: test bit corresponding to entity flag in DAT_680134a8\n6. If flag bit clear, disable callback execution by setting bEnabled = 0\n7. Check entity processing flag: test bit 0x8 in entity flags at returned pointer\n8. If bit 0x8 set (entity already processing), disable callback by setting bEnabled = 0  \n9. Update SEH state to 0 (normal execution)\n10. Conditional execution: if bEnabled != 0, set entity processing flag (OR 0x8) and call FUN_68005b20\n11. Alternative path: if callback needed but bEnabled = 0, execute global callback via DAT_6802100c\n12. Restore exception handling state and return\n\nParameters:\npEntity (GameEntity *) - Pointer to game entity structure with type ID and flags\npfnCallback (int) - Function pointer or callback identifier for processing\nfEnabled (int) - Initial enable flag for callback execution\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if entity flags >= 3 (invalid entity type)\n- Early exit if entity lookup fails (returns NULL pointer)\n- Global flag checking prevents processing based on DAT_680134a8 bit mask\n- Entity flag 0x8 prevents double processing of same entity\n- SEH wrapper provides exception safety for callback execution\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x28 (40) - Offset to entity type ID (ushort) in GameEntity structure\n0x6d (109) - Offset to entity flags (byte) in GameEntity structure  \n0x3 (3) - Maximum valid entity flag value\n0x8 (8) - Entity processing flag bit (prevents double processing)\n0x12 (18) - Message/event type passed to FUN_68005b20\n0x4 (4) - Message size parameter for FUN_68005b20