      "comment": "Outputs debug information for a UnitAny structure to the debug console.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer is not NULL\n2. Call FUN_680061a8 to extract unit field values into local buffer\n3. Output basic unit information using printf-style formatting:\n   - Unit pointer address, ID, Type, BaseId, State, X, Y coordinates\n4. Check if unit type equals 4 (special unit type)\n5. Validate unit has a body pointer (pBody != NULL)\n6. If both conditions met, output detailed body information:\n   - Body value, Page, Owner, CmdFlag, Flag, Level, UID, and byte values\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit: Pointer to UnitAny structure to dump debug information for\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL unit pointer: Function returns immediately without output\n- Unit type != 4: Only basic unit information is displayed\n- Unit type == 4 but no body: Only basic unit information is displayed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x4: Special unit type that has extended body information\n\nStructure Layout:\nUnitAny (24 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field     | Type        | Description\n-------|------|-----------|-------------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwType    | uint        | Unit type (4 = special type)\n0x04   | 4    | dwId      | uint        | Unit identifier\n0x08   | 4    | field_8   | uint        | Reserved field\n0x0C   | 4    | dwBaseId  | uint        | Base unit identifier  \n0x10   | 4    | dwState   | uint        | Current unit state\n0x14   | 4    | pBody     | UnitBody *  | Pointer to body structure\n\nUnitBody (72 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field         | Type | Description\n-------|------|---------------|------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwBodyValue   | uint | Body identifier value\n0x0C   | 4    | dwPage        | uint | Page number\n0x14   | 4    | dwOwner       | uint | Owner identifier\n0x18   | 4    | dwCmdFlag     | uint | Command flags\n0x1C   | 4    | dwFlag        | uint | General flags\n0x20   | 4    | dwLevel       | uint | Level value\n0x44   | 1    | byFirstByte   | byte | First byte value\n0x45   | 1    | bySecondByte  | byte | Second byte value",
