      "comment": "Retrieves width and height dimensions for a unit based on its type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is not NULL\n2. Load type-specific data pointer from unit structure at offset 0x2c\n3. Validate type-specific data pointer is not NULL\n4. Switch on unit type value to determine dimension extraction method:\n   - Types 0,1,3 (small units): Extract ushort values from offsets +2 and +6\n   - Types 2,4,5 (large units): Extract uint values from offsets +0xc and +0x10\n   - Default: Set both dimensions to 0 and return false\n5. Store extracted dimensions in output parameters\n6. Return true for successful extraction\n\nParameters:\npdwUnitType - Input: Pointer to unit type field (uint *), typically &pUnit->dwType\npdwWidth - Output: Pointer to receive unit width dimension (uint *)\npdwHeight - Output: Pointer to receive unit height dimension (uint *)\n\nReturns:\ntrue (1) - Successfully extracted dimensions for valid unit types 0-5\nfalse (0) - Failed due to NULL input, NULL type data pointer, or invalid unit type\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL input parameters: Sets width=0xffffffff, height=0xffffffff, returns false\nInvalid unit type (>5): Sets width=0, height=0, returns false\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0, 0x1, 0x3 - Small unit types using ushort dimensions\n0x2, 0x4, 0x5 - Large unit types using uint dimensions  \n0x2c - Offset to type-specific data pointer in unit structure\n0x2, 0x6 - Offsets for small unit width/height (ushort)\n0xc, 0x10 - Offsets for large unit width/height (uint)\n0xffffffff - Error sentinel value for NULL input",
