      "comment": "Parse anti-cheat configuration data containing address-value pairs\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize address/value buffer arrays (1024 entries) to zero\n2. Reset global counters and status variables to zero\n3. Split configuration data string by comma delimiters into lines array\n4. Process each line in the configuration data:\n   a. First line contains numeric status value (stored in g_dwAntiCheatStatus)\n   b. Skip lines beginning with '#' or ';' (comments)\n   c. Parse remaining lines into address-value pairs using ParseCommandLineArguments\n   d. Validate minimum 2 tokens exist (address and value)\n   e. Convert hexadecimal strings to numeric values using strtoul with base 16\n   f. Store address at g_adAntiCheatAddresses[index], value at g_adAntiCheatValues[index]\n   g. Increment global count (g_dwAntiCheatCount)\n   h. Free token array from parser\n5. Free main lines array from string splitter\n6. Display final status message with count and enabled/disabled state\n\nParameters:\nlpszConfigData (char *): Configuration string containing comma-separated lines\n                        First line: numeric status value\n                        Subsequent lines: \"address,value\" pairs in hexadecimal\n                        Lines starting with '#' or ';' are ignored as comments\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Comments: Lines starting with '#' or ';' are skipped entirely\n- Invalid lines: Lines with less than 2 tokens after parsing are ignored\n- Empty data: Function safely handles NULL or empty configuration strings\n- Buffer limits: Arrays support maximum 1024 address-value pairs\n- Status display: Uses different message strings based on g_dwAntiCheatStatus value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x400 (1024): Maximum entries in address/value arrays\n0x23 (35): ASCII '#' character for comment detection\n0x3b (59): ASCII ';' character for comment detection  \n0x10 (16): Hexadecimal base for strtoul conversion\n0x2 (2): Minimum required tokens per line (address + value)\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL pointer checks on parsing function results\n- Minimum token count validation before processing\n- Safe array indexing using global counter\n- Memory cleanup with free() for all allocated arrays\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\ng_adAntiCheatAddresses[1024]: Array storing hexadecimal memory addresses\ng_adAntiCheatValues[1024]: Array storing corresponding hexadecimal values  \ng_dwAntiCheatCount: Total number of valid address-value pairs loaded\ng_dwAntiCheatStatus: Status flag from first line (0=disabled, non-zero=enabled)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
