      "comment": "Validates game ID and returns pointer to corresponding game entry in global table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game ID exceeds maximum valid value (0x401)\n2. If invalid, log error message with game ID and return NULL pointer\n3. If valid, calculate offset into game entry table using 8-byte stride\n4. Return pointer to game entry at calculated offset\n\nParameters:\nwGameId (ushort) - Game identifier to validate and lookup (0-0x401 valid range)\n\nReturns:\nvoid * - Pointer to GameEntry structure in global table for valid IDs\nnull - For invalid game IDs that exceed 0x401\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGame ID 0x401 is the maximum valid ID (1025 decimal)\nError logging includes format string \"Invalid Game Id: %d\"\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x401 (1025) - Maximum valid game ID threshold\n0x8 (8) - Size in bytes of each GameEntry structure\n0x6800fe00 - Debug log format string pointer\n0x6800fdec - Error message string \"Invalid Game Id: %d\"\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwGameId   | uint | Game identifier\n0x04   | 4    | dwFlags    | uint | Game state flags\n\nError Handling:\nInvalid game ID triggers InitializeDebugLogAndWrite call\nFunction returns NULL for any ID > 0x401\nNo validation for negative values (ushort is unsigned)",
