      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new timing context structure with timestamp tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 64 bytes of memory using VirtualAlloc with MEM_COMMIT (0x1000) and PAGE_READWRITE (0x4)\n2. Validate allocation succeeded, return NULL if failed\n3. Initialize allocated memory to zero using REP STOSD (16 iterations of 4-byte stores)\n4. Set self-pointer at offset 0x00 for validation/debugging\n5. Store input value at offset 0x04 for context identification\n6. Capture start timestamp using GetTickCount and store at offset 0x1c (28)\n7. Capture end timestamp using GetTickCount and store at offset 0x2c (44)\n8. Return pointer to initialized context structure\n\nParameters:\ndwValue - Input value stored in context for identification or configuration\n\nReturns:\nValid TimingContext pointer - Allocated and initialized structure on success\nNULL - Memory allocation failed (insufficient virtual memory available)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVirtualAlloc failure returns NULL immediately without cleanup required\nDouble timestamp capture provides timing interval capability\nSelf-pointer enables structure validation in consumer functions\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type         Description\n0x00    4     pSelf          void*        Self-pointer for validation\n0x04    4     dwValue        uint         Input parameter value\n0x08    24    reserved1      uint[6]      Reserved space for future use\n0x1c    4     dwStartTime    uint         GetTickCount timestamp #1\n0x20    12    reserved2      uint[3]      Reserved space between timestamps\n0x2c    4     dwEndTime      uint         GetTickCount timestamp #2\n0x30    4     reserved3      uint         Final padding to 64 bytes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40 (64) - Total structure allocation size in bytes\n0x1000 (4096) - MEM_COMMIT allocation type flag\n0x4 (4) - PAGE_READWRITE protection flag\n0x10 (16) - REP STOSD iteration count for zero initialization\n0x1c (28) - Offset to start time