      "comment": "Validates client information structure and releases its allocated memory if validation succeeds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if client info pointer is not NULL\n2. Validate self-reference: verify ClientInfo->pSelf == pClientInfo  \n3. If validation fails, log error \"ClientInfo ptr mismatch\" and return\n4. Validate client ID: verify ClientInfo->nClientId == nClientId\n5. If ID validation fails, log error \"Client Id mismatch\" and return  \n6. Release memory using VirtualFree with MEM_RELEASE flag (0x8000)\n\nParameters:\n- pClientInfo: Pointer to ClientInfo structure to validate and release\n- nClientId: Expected client ID for validation\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; function logs errors on validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pClientInfo: Function returns immediately without error\n- Self-reference mismatch: Logs error and returns without cleanup\n- Client ID mismatch: Logs error and returns without cleanup  \n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8000: MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree (complete memory release)\n- 0x6800feb4: Debug message type for pointer validation errors\n- 0x6800fee4: Debug message type for ID validation errors\n\nError Handling:\n- Validation failures call InitializeDebugLogAndWrite for error logging\n- No exceptions thrown; errors handled via logging and early return\n- Memory cleanup only occurs after successful validation\n\nStructure Layout:\nClientInfo structure (32 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type         | Description\n0x00   | 4    | pSelf         | ClientInfo * | Self-reference pointer for validation\n0x04   | 4    | nClientId     | int          | Client identifier for validation\n0x08   | 24   | (remaining)   | byte[24]     | Additional client data fields",
