      "instructions": ["0x68F8|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x68FC|SUB|ESP, 0x400", "0x6902|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x6904|PUSH|EBP", "0x6905|JNZ|0x68006911", "0x6907|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x6909|POP|EBP", "0x690A|ADD|ESP, 0x400", "0x6910|RET|", "0x6911|PUSH|0x43e", "0x6916|MOV|EDX, 0x6800ff28", "0x691B|CALL|dword ptr [0x6801460c]", "0x6921|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x6923|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x6925|JNZ|0x6800692f"],
      "comment": "Validates client session and enforces anti-flood, anti-idle, and anti-cheat policies\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - return 0 if nClientHandle is 0\n2. Allocate context structure (0x43E bytes) using global memory allocator\n3. Extract ClientInfo pointer from context at offset 0x68 and validate non-null\n4. Perform ClientInfo structure validation - check self-pointer and client ID match\n5. Get current system tick count for timeout calculations\n6. Check if kick timeout has expired - if so, dispatch client and return 0\n7. Anti-flood validation - check packet count against 1000 packet limit\n8. Reset packet counter if 1000ms elapsed since last reset\n9. Increment packet count and check against server flood limits (ram0x68010ef0+0x34)\n10. Anti-idle activity check - validate last activity within 30 seconds (0x7530ms)\n11. Anti-cheat validation - check anti-cheat timestamp within 45 seconds (0xAFC8ms)\n12. Format and send kick messages to client based on violation type\n13. Log kick reasons to server using WriteFormattedLogEntry with severity codes\n14. Set kick timeout to current tick + 5000ms for rate limiting\n15. Return 1 for kicks/errors, 0 for success\n\nParameters:\n  nContextId (int): Context identifier used for logging and tracking\n  nClientHandle (int): Client handle or session identifier, 0 indicates invalid client\n\nReturns:\n  0: Success - client validation passed or client dispatched\n  1: Error - client kicked for policy violation or validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Custom kick messages stored in ClientInfo offset 0xC override default cheating message\n  - Packet rate limits configurable via global settings at ram0x68010ef0+0x34\n  - Activity timeout configurable via global settings at ram0x68010ef0+0x3C\n  - Anti-cheat system can be disabled via g_dwAntiCheatStatus global flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x43E (1086): Context structure size in bytes\n  0x68 (104): Offset to ClientInfo pointer in context structure  \n  0x3E8 (1000): Packet rate limit threshold\n  0x3E8 (1000): Packet reset interval in milliseconds\n  0x7530 (30000): Activity timeout in milliseconds (30 seconds)\n  0xAFC8 (45000): Anti-cheat timeout in milliseconds (45 seconds)  \n  0x1388 (5000): Kick timeout duration in milliseconds (5 seconds)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Null context allocation returns 0 (success to prevent crash)\n  - Null ClientInfo logs error and returns 1 (kick client)\n  - ClientInfo pointer mismatch logs error and returns 1 (security violation)\n  - ClientInfo ID mismatch logs error and returns 1 (session corruption)\n  - All kick scenarios log appropriate messages with severity codes 2-3\n\nClientInfo Structure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name        | Type | Description\n  -------|------|-------------------|------|------------------------------------------\n  0x00   | 4    | pSelfPointer      | ptr  | Self-reference for validation\n  0x04   | 4    | nClientId         | int  | Client identifier for session matching\n  0x08   | 4    | (unknown)         | int  | Reserved field\n  0x0C   | 4    | lpszKickMessage   | ptr  | Custom kick message or NULL\n  0x10   | 4    | nPacketCount      | uint | Current packet count for rate limiting\n  0x14   | 4    | dwLastResetTime   | uint | Timestamp of last packet counter reset\n  0x18   | 4    | nCurrentPackets   | uint | Packets since last reset\n  0x1C   | 4    | dwLastActivity    | uint | Timestamp of last client activity\n  0x20   | 4    | dwKickTimeout     | uint | Timestamp when kick timeout expires\n  0x24   | 4    | (unknown)         | uint | Reserved field\n  0x28   | 4    | (unknown)         | uint | Reserved field  \n  0x2C   | 4    | dwAntiCheatTime   | uint | Timestamp of last anti-cheat validation",
