      "comment": "Outputs a formatted hex dump of memory buffer to debug log file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate debug log file handle and buffer pointer are non-null\n2. Calculate total number of 16-byte rows needed (size / 16, rounded up)\n3. For each 16-byte row:\n   a. Print row header with base address offset (format: \"%08X: \")\n   b. Process 4 groups of 4 bytes each:\n      - For each byte in group, check if within buffer bounds\n      - Use IsBadReadPtr to safely validate memory access\n      - Format valid bytes as 2-digit hex (format: \"%02X\")\n      - Display \"??\" for invalid/unreadable memory locations\n      - Print space after each hex value\n   c. Print separator space after each 4-byte group\n   d. Print ASCII representation section:\n      - For each byte in the 16-byte row\n      - Use character type checking (_isctype with 0x157 mask for printable)\n      - Display printable characters as-is, non-printable as '.'\n      - Use space padding for bytes beyond buffer end\n   e. Print newline to complete the row\n4. Flush debug log file to ensure immediate output\n\nParameters:\npBuffer - Base address of memory buffer to dump (void pointer)\ndwSize - Size of buffer in bytes (unsigned integer)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pDebugLogFile is NULL, function returns immediately without output\n- If pBuffer is NULL (0), function returns immediately without output  \n- Buffer size of 0 results in no output but still flushes log file\n- Uses IsBadReadPtr for safe memory access validation\n- Character type mask 0x157 checks for: uppercase, lowercase, digits, punctuation, space\n- Invalid memory locations display as \"??\" in hex section and '.' in ASCII section\n- Bytes beyond buffer end show as spaces in hex section and space in ASCII section\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16) - Bytes displayed per row\n0x4 (4) - Bytes per group in hex display  \n0xf (15) - Mask for extracting remainder in row calculation\n0x157 (343) - Character type mask for printable character detection\n  Bit flags: _UPPER | _LOWER | _DIGIT | _PUNCT | _SPACE\n0x2e ('.') - Replacement character for non-printable bytes\n0x20 (' ') - Space character for padding beyond buffer end\n0x3f ('?') - Replacement character for unreadable memory\n\nError Handling:\n- IsBadReadPtr return value of non-zero indicates invalid memory access\n- Invalid memory access results in \"??\" hex display and '.' ASCII display\n- C runtime locale functions handle multibyte character detection safely\n- Early return prevents crashes when debug file handle or buffer is invalid",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
