      "api_calls": [],
      "instructions": ["0x6DEC|PUSH|EAX", "0x6DED|PUSH|0x68010118", "0x6DF2|PUSH|0x6801013c", "0x6DF7|CALL|0x68006258", "0x6DFC|MOV|EAX, [0x68013250]", "0x6E01|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x6E04|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x6E06|JZ|0x68006e4e", "0x6E08|PUSH|0x0", "0x6E0A|LEA|ECX, [EBP + -0x24]", "0x6E0D|PUSH|0x1c", "0x6E0F|PUSH|ECX", "0x6E10|PUSH|0x0", "0x6E12|PUSH|ESI", "0x6E13|CALL|EAX"],
      "comment": "Dumps comprehensive thread information including basic info, timing data, and stack contents\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if debug logging is enabled via DAT_68013554\n2. Get current thread handle and thread ID using Win32 APIs\n3. Log thread information header with thread ID\n4. Query thread basic information (class 0) via NT API function pointer\n5. Extract and log stack range (base and limit) and affinity mask\n6. Query thread timing information (class 1) via NT API function pointer \n7. Log creation time, kernel time, and user time as 64-bit FILETIME values\n8. Query thread start address (class 9) via NT API function pointer\n9. Log the thread entry point address\n10. Save current processor register state to stack\n11. Log complete register dump (EAX, EBX, ECX, EDX, ESI, EDI, ESP, EBP)\n12. Calculate stack dump parameters using stack range or default 64KB\n13. Determine optimal dump buffer pointer (current stack or stack base)\n14. Perform hex dump of stack memory contents up to 64KB maximum\n15. Log completion message\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nNothing (void)\n\nIMPLICIT:\nGlobal flag DAT_68013554 - Debug logging enabled flag  \nFunction pointer DAT_68013250 - NT API NtQueryInformationThread\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf DAT_68013554 is 0, function returns immediately without logging\nIf NT API function pointer is null, logs \"No thread information available\"\nIf any NT API query fails (returns negative), skips that information section\nStack dump size limited to maximum 0x10000 (65536) bytes\nStack dump starts from current ESP or stack base, whichever is higher\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1c (28) - Size of THREAD_BASIC_INFORMATION structure\n0x20 (32) - Size of THREAD_TIMES structure  \n0x04 (4) - Size of thread start address DWORD\n0x10000 (65536) - Maximum stack dump size in bytes\nClass 0 - ThreadBasicInformation query type\nClass 1 - ThreadTimes query type\nClass 9 - ThreadQuerySetWin32StartAddress query type\n\nStructure Layout:\nTHREAD_BASIC_INFORMATION (28 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type        Description\n0x00    4     ExitStatus        DWORD       Thread exit status (0 if running)\n0x04    4     pStackBase        PVOID       Top of stack memory region\n0x08    4     pStackLimit       PVOID       Bottom of stack memory region  \n0x0c    4     pFiberData        PVOID       Fiber data pointer (usually NULL)\n0x10    4     dwStackReserveSize DWORD      Reserved stack size in bytes\n0x14    4     dwStackCommitSize  DWORD      Committed stack size in bytes\n0x18    8     ClientId          CLIENT_ID   Process ID and Thread ID pair\n\nTHREAD_TIMES (32 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type        Description\n0x00    8     ullCreationTime     FILETIME    Thread creation time\n0x08    8     ullKernelTime       FILETIME    Time spent in kernel mode\n0x10    8     ullUserTime         FILETIME    Time spent in user mode\n0x18    8     ullExitTime         FILETIME    Thread exit time (0 if running)",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_Control"]
