      "comment": "Extracts a type-specific byte property from an object through indirect pointer chain validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input object pointer is not NULL\n2. Check object type field (offset 0) equals 2 for compatibility\n3. Follow pointer at object offset 0x14 to secondary structure\n4. Validate secondary structure pointer is not NULL  \n5. Dereference secondary structure to get tertiary structure pointer\n6. Validate tertiary structure pointer is not NULL\n7. Extract byte value from tertiary structure at offset 0x13a\n8. Zero-extend byte to uint and return result\n\nParameters:\n  pObject (BaseObject *) - Source object to extract property from, must have type field = 2\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Zero-extended byte value from offset 0x13a of tertiary structure\n  0 - If any validation fails (NULL pointers or wrong object type)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Type field validation (offset 0): Must equal 2, returns 0 if different\n  - Three-level pointer chain validation: Any NULL pointer returns 0\n  - Byte extraction: Single byte at offset 0x13a (314 decimal) zero-extended to uint\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2 (2) - Required object type for compatibility validation\n  0x14 (20) - Offset to secondary structure pointer in BaseObject\n  0x13a (314) - Offset to target byte property in tertiary structure",
