      "comment": "Generates a pseudo-random seed value based on system tick count with overflow handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system tick count from GetTickCount()\n2. Check if current ticks < previous ticks (overflow condition)\n3. If overflow detected, increment overflow counter\n4. Store current tick count in global RNG state structure\n5. Store tick count bytes individually for seeding purposes\n6. Calculate and return composite random value using:\n   - Overflow count * 0x41893 (magic multiplier)\n   - Base seed value from RNG state\n   - Normalized time delta / 1000\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint - Pseudo-random seed value combining tick count, overflow handling, and base state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x41893 - Random number generator multiplier constant\n0x10624dd3 - Division constant for /1000 optimization (reciprocal multiplication)\n1000 - Time normalization divisor (milliseconds to seconds conversion)\n\nGlobal State Access:\ng_rngState structure at 0x68013230:\n- +0x00: Base seed value (dwSeedBase)\n- +0x04: Previous tick count (dwPreviousTicks) \n- +0x08: Current tick count (dwCurrentTicks)\n- +0x0C: Overflow counter (dwOverflowCount)\n- +0x60-0x63: Individual tick count bytes for seeding",
