      "comment": "Loads item configuration data from specified file path.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameter is not NULL and not empty string\n2. Copy file path to global buffer at offset 0x7c (max 260 bytes)\n3. Clear termination flag at 0x68013357\n4. Check if buffer contains valid path data\n5. Call configuration preparation function FUN_680087d0()\n6. Attempt to load item data from file using FUN_680081a0()\n7. Log success with item count or failure message via logging handler\n\nParameters:\n  lpszConfigPath: Pointer to null-terminated file path string for item data\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Number of items loaded from configuration file (> 0)\n  Failure: 0 if path invalid, empty, or load operation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL or empty path returns 0 immediately\n  - Maximum path length is 260 characters (0x104 bytes)\n  - Termination flag cleared regardless of load success/failure\n  - Logging performed through global function pointer _g_pfnLogHandler\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x104 (260): Maximum path buffer size for file operations\n  0x7c (124): Offset into global formatted string buffer for path storage\n  0x68013254: Global path buffer start address\n  0x68013357: Termination flag byte location",
