      "comment": "Load and initialize World Event configuration from specified file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input configuration file path parameter for null/empty\n2. Copy configuration path to global buffer with strncpy (0x104 byte limit)\n3. Test file accessibility using _access system call with mode 0 (read access)\n4. If file inaccessible, log error and return failure (0)\n5. Clear update processing flag and log configuration load start message\n6. Read UpdateInterval setting and convert to milliseconds (multiply by 1000)\n7. Parse Difficulty setting string and split by delimiter\n8. Process difficulty tokens in loop: \"normal\"=0x01, \"nightmare\"=0x02, \"hell\"=0x04\n9. Combine difficulty flags with OR operations into global enable flags\n10. Free token memory after processing difficulty list\n11. Read SpawnMinions boolean flag and store in message handler enabled flag\n12. Load item generation range settings (min/max values)\n13. Load stat pair values for Normal/Nightmare/Hell game and player factors\n14. Initialize item data system if not already loaded\n15. Read ItemDataFile path and call item initialization function if specified\n16. Load item system handle and log success/failure status\n17. Read Enable boolean flag and store in global update processing enabled\n18. Log final World Event enabled/disabled status message\n19. Execute debug dump thread handler if configured\n20. Return function pointer execution result\n\nParameters:\nlpszConfigPath (char *): Path to configuration INI file containing World Event settings\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Non-zero value from executed function pointer or initialization routine\nFailure: 0 if file access failed, null pointer provided, or empty path string\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction uses indirect jump through global function pointer at end for modular execution\nFile must be accessible with read permissions or function exits early with error\nEmpty/null configuration path causes immediate failure return without processing\nDifficulty string parsing supports multiple comma-separated values combined with bitwise OR\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x104 (260): Maximum configuration file path length in bytes\n1000: Millisecond conversion factor for update interval timing\n0x01: Normal difficulty enable flag (bit 0)\n0x02: Nightmare difficulty enable flag (bit 1) \n0x04: Hell difficulty enable flag (bit 2)\n0x400 (1024): Configuration value buffer size for string reads\n0x80 (128): Item file path maximum length\n\nStructure Layout:\nStatPair structure (8 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | nValue1    | int  | Player factor value\n0x04   | 4    | nValue2    | int  | Game factor value",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
