      "comment": "Reads a configuration value from an INI file if game server mode is enabled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize buffer to empty string if buffer pointer is valid\n2. Validate section parameter is not null\n3. Validate key parameter is not null  \n4. Check if game server flag is enabled (g_bGameServerFlag != 0)\n5. Call GetPrivateProfileStringA with section, key, empty default, buffer, size, and server flag as filename\n6. Return true if buffer contains data after call, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\nlpszSection (LPCSTR): INI file section name to read from\nlpszKey (LPCSTR): Key name within section to retrieve\nlpszBuffer (LPSTR): Output buffer to receive the value string\ndwBufferSize (DWORD): Maximum size of output buffer in characters\nIMPLICIT: Uses g_bGameServerFlag global to determine server filename\n\nReturns:\ntrue: Configuration value was successfully read and buffer contains data\nfalse: Failed due to null parameters, server mode disabled, or no value found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns false immediately if any input parameter is null\n- Returns false if g_bGameServerFlag is 0 (server mode disabled)  \n- Buffer is always null-terminated even on failure\n- Uses empty string (&g_szDefaultValue) as default value for GetPrivateProfileStringA\n\nError Handling:\n- Null parameter validation prevents crashes\n- Game server flag check prevents file access when not in server mode\n- Empty string initialization ensures buffer always has valid null termination",
