      "comment": "Parse numeric value from INI configuration file using section and key parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 32-byte temporary buffer on stack for configuration value\n2. Call ReadConfigValue with section, key, buffer, and buffer size (0x20 = 32 bytes)\n3. Convert resulting string buffer to unsigned long integer using strtoul with base 0 (auto-detect)\n4. Discard conversion result (function performs parsing but doesn't return value)\n\nParameters:\nlpszFirstValue (char*): INI file section name to read from\nlpszSecondValue (char*): Key name within section to retrieve value for\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function performs parsing operation but discards result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size fixed at 32 bytes (0x20) for configuration value storage\n- Uses strtoul base 0 for automatic base detection (hex with 0x, octal with 0, decimal otherwise)\n- Conversion result is computed but not returned or stored\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20 (32): Fixed buffer size for configuration value string storage\n0x0 (0): Base parameter for strtoul enabling automatic base detection\n\nError Handling:\n- ReadConfigValue handles null parameter validation and server mode checking\n- strtoul handles invalid string format gracefully (returns 0)\n- No error propagation since function returns void",
