      "comment": "Validates whether a configuration key-value string pair can be successfully parsed as an unsigned integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Pass the configuration key and value strings to ParseStringPairToUnsigned for processing\n2. Check if the parsing operation returned a non-zero result (success indicator)\n3. Convert the non-zero/zero result to boolean true/false using bitwise operations\n4. Return validation result to caller\n\nParameters:\nlpszConfigKey - Configuration key string to locate the value\nlpszConfigValue - Configuration value string to parse as unsigned integer\n\nReturns:\ntrue - Configuration pair was successfully parsed as unsigned integer\nfalse - Configuration pair parsing failed (invalid format, missing key, etc.)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses assembly bitwise operations (NEG, SBB, NEG) to convert non-zero to 1, zero stays 0",
