      "comment": "Loads game statistics data from external source and initializes global timing variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local buffer array (4 integers) for statistics data retrieval\n2. Call FUN_68007eb0 to load statistics data into local buffer\n3. Check function return status using phantom high bits combined with boolean result\n4. If data load failed (non-zero status): clear entire buffer with REP STOSD and set return code to 0\n5. If data load succeeded: set return code to 1\n6. Copy loaded values from buffer to global variables:\n   - anStatisticsBuffer[3] -> g_nBaseStat1DefaultValue (base stat default)\n   - dwBaseStat1 -> g_nBaseStat1 (current base stat value)\n   - dwProcessingStartTime -> g_dwProcessingStartTime (processing timestamp)\n   - dwTimeConditionTimestamp -> g_dwTimeConditionTimestamp (condition timer)\n   - dwExecutionCounter -> g_dwExecutionCounter (execution counter)\n7. Set global completion flag DAT_68013460 to 1\n8. Return success/failure status\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n0 (uint) - Statistics data loaded and globals initialized successfully\n1 (uint) - Failed to load statistics data, globals cleared to defaults\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses CONCAT31 with extraout_var to check 32-bit return value where only low byte is boolean\nREP STOSD efficiently clears 8 DWORDs (32 bytes) when load fails\nGlobal flag DAT_68013460 always set to 1 regardless of load success/failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 (8) - Number of DWORDs to clear in buffer (32 bytes total)\n0x1 (1) - Success indicator for completion flag\n0x0 (0) - Return code for successful data load\n0x1 (1) - Return code for failed data load",
