      "comment": "Validates the header of the D2GEVar.dat game statistics file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if header pointer is not NULL, return false if NULL\n2. Open D2GEVar.dat file in binary read mode (\"rb\")\n3. Return false if file cannot be opened\n4. Read exactly 32 bytes from file into header structure\n5. Close file handle after reading\n6. Return false if read size != 32 bytes (incomplete read)\n7. Validate magic number field (offset 0x0) == 0x33445566\n8. Return false if magic number is invalid\n9. Validate version field (offset 0x4) == 0x1001001\n10. Return false if version is unsupported\n11. Calculate checksum using FUN_68007f40 on header data\n12. Compare calculated checksum against stored checksum (offset 0x8)\n13. Return true if checksums match, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npHeader (GameStatisticsHeader *): Pointer to 32-byte header structure to validate\n\nReturns:\ntrue: Header is valid (magic, version, and checksum all correct)\nfalse: Header validation failed (NULL pointer, file error, or validation mismatch)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x33445566 (862341478 decimal): Expected magic number signature\n- 0x1001001 (16781313 decimal): Required version identifier\n- 0x20 (32 decimal): Expected header size in bytes\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwMagic       uint    File signature (0x33445566)\n0x04    4     dwVersion     uint    Format version (0x1001001)\n0x08    4     dwChecksum    uint    Validation checksum\n0x0C    20    abReserved    byte[]  Reserved for future expansion\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL pointer check prevents segmentation fault\n- File open failure indicates missing or inaccessible D2GEVar.dat\n- Incomplete read suggests file corruption or truncation\n- Magic/version mismatch indicates wrong file format or version\n- Checksum failure indicates data corruption or tampering",
