      "comment": "Releases reference-counted buffer resources from a dual buffer management structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check secondary buffer at offset 0x14 - if not NULL, examine reference count at buffer[-1]\n2. If reference count is 0 or -1 (0xFF), call operator_delete to free the buffer memory\n3. Otherwise decrement reference count by 1 and continue using the buffer\n4. Clear secondary buffer descriptor fields (pData, dwSize, dwCapacity) to zero\n5. Check primary buffer at offset 0x4 - if not NULL, examine reference count at buffer[-1] \n6. If reference count is 0 or -1 (0xFF), call operator_delete to free the buffer memory\n7. Otherwise decrement reference count by 1 and continue using the buffer\n8. Clear primary buffer descriptor fields (pData, dwSize, dwCapacity) to zero\n\nParameters:\npBufferManager (DualBufferManager *): Pointer to structure containing two buffer descriptors\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (cleanup function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL buffer pointers are safely ignored (no-op)\n- Reference count of 0 indicates last reference, triggers deletion\n- Reference count of -1 (0xFF) indicates deletion marker, triggers deletion\n- Reference counting uses byte storage at buffer address minus 1\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type              | Description\n-------|------|------------------|-------------------|---------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwFlags          | uint              | Management flags (unused here)\n0x04   | 12   | primaryBuffer    | BufferDescriptor  | Primary buffer information  \n0x10   | 12   | secondaryBuffer  | BufferDescriptor  | Secondary buffer information\n\nBufferDescriptor Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type    | Description\n-------|------|-------------|---------|---------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | pData       | char *  | Pointer to buffer data\n0x04   | 4    | dwSize      | uint    | Current buffer size\n0x08   | 4    | dwCapacity  | uint    | Maximum buffer capacity\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFF (-1): Reference count deletion marker indicating buffer marked for deletion\n0x00 (0): Reference count indicating this is the last reference to the buffer",
