      "comment": "Parses a comma-separated list of names and adds them to the global processing queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception handling frame and two basic_string objects for name processing\n2. Validate input string is not null or empty\n3. Create working copy of input string using operator_new\n4. Parse input for path separator (0x2f '/') and remove path portion\n5. Parse input for colon separator (0x3a ':') to separate name from extension  \n6. If extension found, copy global extension string (g_szFileExtension) to extension buffer\n7. Process extension characters: skip whitespace, convert to lowercase using tolower()\n8. Loop through comma-separated names in reverse order using strrchr(0x2c ','):\n   a. Find last comma and null-terminate to isolate current name\n   b. Skip leading whitespace using isspace() \n   c. Trim trailing whitespace from end of name\n   d. Copy trimmed name to local string buffer\n   e. Allocate new ListNode using FUN_68008fa0 (list insertion)\n   f. Copy name string to node using FUN_68008fd0 (string copy)\n   g. Increment global list counter g_dwListCount\n9. Continue until no more commas found (reaches beginning of string)\n10. Clean up allocated memory using operator_delete\n11. Destroy string objects and restore exception frame\n\nParameters:\nlpszNameList - Input string containing comma-separated list of names to process\n\nReturns:\n1 (true) - Successfully processed all names and added to queue\n0 (false) - Failed due to null input, empty string, or memory allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null or empty input returns 0 immediately\n- Path separators (/) are removed, keeping only filename portion  \n- Colon separators (:) split name from extension\n- Leading/trailing whitespace is trimmed from each name\n- Memory allocation failure during processing returns 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2f (47) - Forward slash '/' path separator\n0x3a (58) - Colon ':' name/extension separator  \n0x2c (44) - Comma ',' name lis