      "comment": "Processes an input string by converting characters to lowercase and handling special sequences.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Input validation - return NULL if input string is NULL\n2. Initialize two local string objects for processing\n3. Calculate input string length using strlen-like loop (0xffffffff initial count)\n4. Calculate global string constant length from g_szFileExtension\n5. Allocate string buffer and copy global string constant as base\n6. Iterate through each character of input string:\n   a. Check for forward slash ('/') - if found, terminate processing\n   b. Call SearchStringInList for special sequence processing\n   c. If special sequence found, append result and advance by sequence length\n   d. Otherwise, check if character is whitespace using isspace()\n   e. If not whitespace, convert to lowercase using tolower() and append\n7. Allocate result buffer using OperatorNew (input_length + 1 bytes)\n8. Copy processed string content to result buffer\n9. Clean up temporary string objects with reference counting\n10. Return pointer to allocated result string\n\nParameters:\n\nlpszInput: Input string to process (NULL returns NULL)\n\nReturns:\n\nPointer to dynamically allocated result string containing lowercase version\nNULL if input is NULL or memory allocation fails\nCaller responsible for freeing returned pointer with OperatorDelete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nProcessing stops at first forward slash ('/') character\nWhitespace characters are skipped during processing\nGlobal string constant g_szFileExtension used as processing base\nMemory allocation failure returns NULL after cleanup\nReference counting cleanup for std::string objects\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xffffffff: Initial value for strlen calculation loop\n0x2f: Forward slash character ('/') that terminates processing\n0x0: NULL pointer checks and string termination\n\nError Handling:\n\nReturns NULL if lpszInput parameter is NULL\nReturns NULL if memory allocation fails (OperatorNew)