      "comment": "Searches for a string match in a global linked list of string entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize match length output parameter to 0\n2. Calculate input string length using REPNE SCASB scan\n3. Return false immediately if input string is empty (length 0)\n4. Iterate through global linked list starting from g_pListHead->pNext\n5. For each list node, extract string data pointer from abData+4 offset\n6. Use null pointer fallback to _C_exref if data pointer is null\n7. Perform case-insensitive comparison using _strnicmp with entry length\n8. If comparison result > 0, continue to next node (alphabetical ordering)\n9. If comparison result < 0, break loop (passed potential match point)\n10. If exact match found (result == 0) and current match length < entry length:\n    a. Get maximum copy length from npos_exref and entry string length\n    b. Use minimum of the two values as actual copy length\n    c. If result string equals entry string object, erase existing content\n    d. Otherwise, check if copy length equals entry length for direct assignment\n    e. For direct assignment, verify reference count < 0xFE, then _Tidy and copy\n    f. For partial copy, use _Grow to allocate space and perform DWORD+byte copy\n    g. Update match length to entry length from abData+0x20 offset\n11. If match length equals input string length, return true (exact match)\n12. Continue to next node via pNext pointer until back to list head\n13. Return true if any match found (match length > 0), false otherwise\n\nParameters:\nlpszSearchString - Input string to search for in the list\npnMatchLength - Output pointer to receive length of longest match found\npResultString - Output std::string object to receive matched string data\nIMPLICIT: None\n\nReturns:\ntrue - String match found, match length and result string populated\nfalse - No match found, output parameters may be partially modified\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty input string returns false immediately\nNull data pointers in