      "comment": "Dynamically resolves procedure addresses from modules with dual resolution modes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Attempt to get existing module handle using GetModuleHandleA(lpszModuleName)\n2. If module not already loaded, load it using LoadLibraryA(lpszModuleName)\n3. Return NULL (0x0) if both module handle and library loading fail\n4. Check resolution mode based on nOrdinalOrOffset sign:\n   - If negative: Resolve by ordinal using GetProcAddress(hModule, -nOrdinalOrOffset)\n   - If positive: Resolve by direct offset calculation (hModule.base + nOrdinalOrOffset)\n5. Return resolved function pointer or calculated address\n\nParameters:\n  lpszModuleName (LPCSTR) - Name of the module/DLL to resolve procedures from\n  nOrdinalOrOffset (int) - Dual-mode parameter:\n                          - Negative values: Function ordinal number (negated)\n                          - Positive values: Byte offset from module base address\n\nReturns:\n  FARPROC - Function pointer to resolved procedure\n  NULL (0x0) - Module could not be loaded or found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nOrdinalOrOffset == 0: Returns module base address (hModule.base + 0)\n  - Negative values trigger ordinal-based API resolution via GetProcAddress\n  - Positive values bypass API and calculate direct memory addresses\n  - Uses hModule->unused field as base for offset calculations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x0 (NULL) - Failure indicator for module loading and return value",
