      "comment": "Validates target object using configurable comparison operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate comparison configuration has valid function pointer at offset 0x4\n2. Validate target object pointer is not NULL\n3. Validate target object has valid validation handle at offset 0x14\n4. Call comparison function with target object and additional parameter from offset 0xc\n5. Switch on comparison type from offset 0x8 to determine validation logic\n6. Compare function result with expected value from offset 0x10 based on operation type\n7. Return TRUE if comparison matches criteria, FALSE otherwise\n\nParameters:\nthis (ComparisonConfig *): Pointer to comparison configuration structure\n  - Offset 0x4: Function pointer for comparison operation\n  - Offset 0x8: Comparison type selector (1-5)  \n  - Offset 0xc: Additional parameter passed to comparison function\n  - Offset 0x10: Expected comparison value\npComparisonConfig (ComparisonConfig *): First parameter (this pointer in __thiscall)\npTargetObject (TargetObject *): Pointer to target object being validated\n  - Offset 0x14: Validation handle (must be non-NULL)\npValidationTarget (void *): Additional parameter (calling convention artifact)\n\nReturns:\nbool: TRUE if target object passes comparison validation, FALSE otherwise\n- FALSE if any validation check fails (NULL pointers, invalid handles)\n- FALSE if comparison type is invalid (not 1-5)\n- Result of comparison operation based on type:\n  - Type 1: dwComparisonResult == dwExpectedValue (equality)\n  - Type 2: dwComparisonResult < dwExpectedValue (less than)\n  - Type 3: dwExpectedValue < dwComparisonResult (greater than)\n  - Type 4: dwExpectedValue >= dwComparisonResult (greater than or equal)\n  - Type 5: dwComparisonResult >= dwExpectedValue (less than or equal)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNULL validation handles cause immediate FALSE return\nInvalid comparison types (>5) fall through to FALSE return\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4 - Function pointer offset in comparison config\n0x8 - Comparison type offset in comparison config  \n0xc - Additional parameter offset in comparison config\n0x10 - Expected value offset in comparison config\n0x14 - Validation handle offset in target object\n1-5 - Valid comparison type values\n\nStructure Layout:\nComparisonConfig:\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type   | Description\n0x0    | 4    | Unknown             | dword  | Reserved/padding\n0x4    | 4    | pComparatorFunction | void*  | Function pointer for comparison\n0x8    | 4    | nComparisonType     | dword  | Operation type (1-5)\n0xc    | 4    | dwAdditionalParam   | dword  | Parameter passed to function\n0x10   | 4    | dwComparisonValue   | dword  | Expected comparison value\n\nTargetObject:\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type   | Description  \n0x0    | 20   | Unknown Fields      | bytes  | Object-specific data\n0x14   | 4    | pValidationHandle   | void*  | Validation handle (NULL check)",
