      "comment": "Creates a parser object based on delimiter characters found in a configuration string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input string parameter for null pointer\n2. Initialize structured exception handling (SEH) frame\n3. Search for pipe delimiter '|' (0x7c) using strchr\n4. If pipe not found, search for semicolon ';' (0x3b)\n5. If semicolon not found, search for ampersand '&' (0x26)  \n6. If ampersand not found, search for comma ',' (0x2c)\n7. If no delimiter found, create single-item parser via FUN_68009920\n8. If delimiter found, create multi-item parser via FUN_68009790\n9. Set parser delimiter character at offset +0x4\n10. Set parser mode at offset +0x8 (1=single, 2=multi)\n11. Initialize parser by calling virtual function at offset +0x0\n12. Return parser object on success, cleanup and return NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n- lpszConfigString: Input configuration string to parse for delimiters\n\nReturns:\n- Parser pointer on successful creation and initialization  \n- NULL if input string is null or parser initialization fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Delimiter precedence: pipe > semicolon > ampersand > comma\n- Single-item mode (1) for comma delimiter\n- Multi-item mode (2) for all other delimiters\n- Parser cleanup via FUN_680097b0 or FUN_68009940 on initialization failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x7c: Pipe character '|' (highest precedence delimiter)\n- 0x3b: Semicolon character ';' \n- 0x26: Ampersand character '&'\n- 0x2c: Comma character ',' (single-item mode)\n- 0x14: Parser object size (20 bytes)\n- Mode 1: Single-item parsing (comma delimiter)\n- Mode 2: Multi-item parsing (all other delimiters)\n\nError Handling:\n- Null input validation at function entry\n- Exception handling via structured exception frames\n- Memory allocation failure checks for operator_new\n- Parser initialization failure detection via virtual function call\n- Automatic cleanup and memory deallocation on any failure path\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field 