      "comment": "Validates handler configuration and dispatches event processing to appropriate handler based on handler type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Validate handler configuration by checking for null pointers\n   - Check if pPrimaryHandler (offset +0xc) is not null\n   - Check if pSecondaryHandler (offset +0x10) is not null\n   - Check if nHandlerType (offset +0x8) is not zero\n\n2. Determine processing mode based on handler type value\n   - If nHandlerType == 1: Use primary-first processing mode\n   - If nHandlerType == 2: Use secondary-first processing mode\n   - Any other value returns false (invalid handler type)\n\n3. Execute primary handler processing for mode 1\n   - Call virtual function at pPrimaryHandler->vtable[1] with dwEventCode\n   - If call succeeds (non-zero), proceed to secondary handler\n   - If call fails (zero), return false immediately\n\n4. Execute secondary handler processing for mode 2\n   - Call virtual function at pPrimaryHandler->vtable[1] with dwEventCode\n   - If call succeeds (non-zero), return true immediately\n   - If call fails (zero), proceed to secondary handler\n\n5. Execute secondary handler as fallback/continuation\n   - Call virtual function at pSecondaryHandler->vtable[1] with dwEventCode\n   - Return true if call succeeds (non-zero), false if fails (zero)\n\nParameters:\n\nthis: Pointer to HandlerDispatcher structure containing handler configuration\ndwEventCode: Event identifier passed to handler virtual functions\n\nReturns:\n\ntrue: Event processing succeeded via primary or secondary handler\nfalse: Event processing failed due to:\n  - Invalid handler configuration (null pointers)\n  - Invalid handler type (not 1 or 2)\n  - Handler function returned failure code (zero)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nHandler Type Values:\n- 0x01: Primary-first mode - try primary handler, then secondary if primary succeeds\n- 0x02: Secondary-first mode - try primary handler, return immediately if succeeds, else try secondary\n- Other: Invalid mode, returns false immediately\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nHandlerDispatcher (20 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name         | Type  | Description\n0x00   | 4    | vtable            | void* | Virtual function table pointer (inherited)\n0x04   | 4    | reserved          | uint  | Reserved field\n0x08   | 4    | nHandlerType      | uint  | Handler processing mode (1 or 2)\n0x0C   | 4    | pPrimaryHandler   | void* | Primary event handler object\n0x10   | 4    | pSecondaryHandler | void* | Secondary/fallback handler object\n\nError Handling:\n\n- Null pointer validation prevents crashes from invalid handler objects\n- Handler type validation ensures only supported modes are processed\n- Virtual function call failures are propagated as boolean return values\n- No exception handling - relies on proper handler object initialization",
