      "comment": "Executes a callback function repeatedly with parameter manipulation within structured exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up structured exception handling (SEH) frame with exception list chaining\n2. Initialize SEH frame with handler function pointer and exception data\n3. Configure exception flags and save previous exception list pointer\n4. Enter main execution loop with iteration counter check\n5. Decrement iteration count and validate remaining iterations\n6. If iterations remain, execute callback function pointer indirectly\n7. Continue loop until all iterations completed (count reaches negative)\n8. Restore previous exception handling state\n9. Clean up SEH frame and return to caller\n\nParameters:\nfDecrementValue (BOOL): Value subtracted from base value during parameter manipulation\nfBaseValue (BOOL): Base value used for parameter calculations in callback context\nnIterationCount (int): Number of times to execute the callback function\npCallback (void*): Function pointer to callback routine executed each iteration\nIMPLICIT: Uses standard Windows SEH with ExceptionList and handler chaining\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value, completion indicated by normal return\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If iteration count is zero or negative initially, loop exits immediately\n- Callback function receives manipulated parameters (fDecrementValue - fBaseValue)\n- SEH protects against exceptions during callback execution\n- Exception handling restored even if callback throws exception\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x68009a50 - SEH exception handler function address\n0x6800b340 - Global exception data structure address\n0xffffffff - SEH completion flag value\n\nError Handling:\n- Structured exception handling protects callback execution\n- Exception list properly restored in all exit paths\n- Handler function manages unhandled exceptions during callback\n- No explicit error return codes, relies on SEH for exception management\n\nStructure Lay