      "comment": "Visual C++ exception filter that terminates process on VC++ runtime exceptions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference ppExceptionInfo to get exception information pointer\n2. Dereference again to access exception record structure  \n3. Compare exception code with Visual C++ runtime exception code (0xe06d7363)\n4. If not VC++ exception, return 0 (continue search)\n5. If VC++ exception detected, call terminate() to abort process\n6. Return extraout_EAX (unreachable due to terminate())\n\nParameters:\nppExceptionInfo (void **): Double pointer to exception information structure\n    First dereference gets PEXCEPTION_POINTERS\n    Second dereference gets PEXCEPTION_RECORD\n    Contains exception code at offset 0x0\n\nReturns:\n0: Exception is not a VC++ runtime exception, continue exception search\nNever returns on VC++ exceptions: terminate() aborts the process\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0xe06d7363 is Microsoft Visual C++ runtime exception code\nEquivalent to signed value -0x1f928c9d in the comparison\nterminate() never returns, making extraout_EAX unreachable\n\nError Handling:\nNo error checking performed - assumes valid pointers\nRelies on Windows SEH mechanism for invalid memory access protection",
