      "comment": "Invokes a callback function multiple times with structured exception handling protection\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize SEH (Structured Exception Handling) frame\n   - Push exception handler address (0x68009a50) and data pointer (DAT_6800b350)\n   - Link to existing exception chain via FS:[0x0]\n   - Set up local exception variables\n\n2. Execute protected callback loop\n   - Initialize loop counter (nLoopIndex = 0)\n   - While nLoopIndex < nCount:\n     a. Load first parameter value into ESI register\n     b. Call function pointer pfnCallback with first parameter\n     c. Add stride value to first parameter for next iteration\n     d. Increment loop counter\n     e. Continue until all callbacks executed\n\n3. Clean up and restore state\n   - Set SEH state to success (0x1)\n   - Mark exception handling complete (0xffffffff)\n   - Call cleanup function FUN_68009eda\n   - Restore previous exception chain\n   - Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n\nnFirstParam - Initial parameter value passed to callback function\nnStride - Increment value added to parameter between iterations  \nnCount - Number of times to invoke the callback function\npfnCallback - Pointer to callback function taking single integer parameter\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nIf nCount <= 0, no callbacks are executed but SEH cleanup still occurs\nException handler at 0x68009a50 protects against callback failures\nDAT_6800b350 contains exception handling data structure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x68009a50 - Address of SEH exception handler function\n0x6800b350 - Global exception data structure address  \n0x1 - SEH success state indicator\n0xffffffff - SEH completion marker for normal exit",
