      "comment": "Cleanup and shutdown game server by releasing all active game sessions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize game entry index to 0\n2. Loop through all possible game entries (0 to 0x401 = 1025 entries)\n3. Call ValidateGameIdAndGetEntry to retrieve game entry pointer for current index\n4. If game entry exists and has allocated memory at offset +4:\n   a. Call free() to deallocate memory pointed to by entry+4\n   b. Clear the pointer at offset +4 to prevent double-free\n5. Increment game entry index and continue until all entries processed\n6. Call D2GSServerShutdown to perform final server cleanup\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Game entries with NULL pointers are skipped without error\n- Game entries with NULL memory at offset +4 are skipped\n- Maximum game entries processed: 0x402 (1026 decimal)\n- Function uses __stdcall calling convention\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x402 (1026) - Maximum number of game sessions supported by server\n0x4 - Offset to allocated memory pointer within game entry structure",
