      "comment": "Initialize Game Server Function Hooks and Dynamic Import Resolution\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global patching completion flag to indicate initialization start\n2. Preserve all registers via PUSHAD for server initialization call  \n3. Execute server initialization with version identification strings\n4. Restore registers and setup hook table metadata (size = 6)\n5. Install first batch of function pointer hooks by backing up originals and replacing with hook addresses\n6. Store game state pointer in global variable for cross-module access\n7. Dynamically resolve imported functions via GetProcAddress using ordinal numbers\n8. Install second batch of function pointer hooks with additional server functionality\n9. Set global entity lookup table pointer for game object management\n10. Call initialization routine for extended function pointer setup\n11. Return module handle to caller for reference\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ESI: pGameState - Pointer to game state structure passed via ESI register for initialization context\n\nReturns:\nvoid * hModule - Module handle (HMODULE) from dynamic library load operation\n                Returns base address of loaded DLL module for caller reference\n                NULL indicates initialization failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction operates with implicit parameter in ESI register requiring register-based calling convention\nPUSHAD/POPAD sequence preserves register state during critical initialization phase\nHook installation replaces function pointers in live function tables requiring atomic operations\nDynamic imports resolved by ordinal numbers rather than function names for obfuscation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6 - Hook table size identifier for metadata validation\n0x2aa8 (10920) - Ordinal for GetPlayerData function import\n0x2b83 (11139) - Ordinal for second dynamically loaded function  \n0x28fe (10494) - Ordinal for third dynamically loaded function\n0x2add (10973) - Ordinal for fourth dynamically loaded function\n0x2b52 (11090) - Ordinal for fifth dynamically loaded function\n0x2a87 (10887) - Ordinal for sixth dynamically loaded function\n0x2a40 (10816) - Ordinal for seventh dynamically loaded function\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking on GetProcAddress calls assumes all imports will resolve successfully\nHook installation proceeds without validation of resolved function addresses\nCaller must verify returned module handle validity and check patching completion flag\nFunction pointer backup allows restoration if hooks need to be removed\n\nState Machine:\nState 1: Global Reset → Clear patching flag, prepare for initialization\nState 2: Version Exchange → Execute server init with identification strings  \nState 3: Hook Table Setup → Configure metadata and install first batch hooks\nState 4: Dynamic Resolution → Resolve external functions by ordinal imports\nState 5: Extended Hooks → Install remaining hooks for complete functionality\nState 6: Completion → Finalize setup and return module reference",
