      "comment": "Initialize game server state and reset server control blocks to defaults.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call InitializeGameServer via function pointer to establish base server state\n2. If initialization fails (return 0), exit early with failure code\n3. Zero out 40-byte server initialization block starting at g_ServerInitBlock\n4. Set callback function pointer at offset 0x14 to NoOpStubFunction placeholder\n5. Call FUN_68022ccd with registration handle for additional server setup\n6. Return final registration status from server setup completion\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no input parameters\n\nReturns:\nuint - Server initialization status code\n  0: Initialization failed (InitializeGameServer returned failure)  \n  Non-zero: Success value from final server setup (dwReturnAddress)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return with 0 if InitializeGameServer fails\n- Uses NoOpStubFunction (0x68001a90) as placeholder callback implementation\n- Function pointer at 0x68021116 indirectly calls InitializeGameServer\n- FUN_68022ccd receives ECX register output as registration handle\n\nStructure Layout:\nServerInitializationBlock g_ServerInitBlock @ 0x680135a0 (40 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-------|----------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | dwField00     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x04   | 4    | dwField04     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)  \n0x08   | 4    | dwField08     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x0C   | 4    | dwField0C     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x10   | 4    | dwField10     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x14   | 4    | pfnCallback   | void* | Callback function pointer (set to NoOpStubFunction)\n0x18   | 4    | dwField18     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x1C   | 4    | dwField1C     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x20   | 4    | dwField20     | uint  | General purpose field (zeroed)\n0x24   | 4  