      "instructions": ["0x21929|PUSHAD|", "0x2192A|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x68021126]", "0x21930|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x21932|PUSH|ESI", "0x21933|PUSH|0x0", "0x21935|CALL|0x68023471", "0x2193A|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x2193C|ADD|ECX, 0xebb55", "0x21942|MOV|AX, 0x9090", "0x21946|MOV|word ptr [ECX], AX", "0x21949|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0x2194B|ADD|ECX, 0xfa3a8", "0x21951|MOV|EAX, 0x6802332e", "0x21956|MOV|dword ptr [ECX], EAX", "0x21958|MOV|ECX, ESI"],
      "comment": "Runtime binary patcher that applies multiple code modifications to loaded DLL modules\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve base address from global pointer DAT_68021126 for primary module patching\n2. Call FUN_68023471 to prepare patching context for primary module\n3. Apply NOP patches (0x9090) to disable existing instructions at 0xebb55 offset\n4. Install function pointer hooks by setting addresses in jump tables (0xfa3a8, 0xfa5f0, 0xfa5f4)\n5. Patch individual instruction bytes to modify opcodes (0x31, 0x2c, 0xeb at various offsets)\n6. Calculate and install relative jump addresses using formula: target - (base + offset)\n7. Set up data structure pointers for runtime lookup tables\n8. If DAT_68021355 flag enabled, copy 47 bytes (0x2f) from source to target buffer with size calculation\n9. Apply conditional patches based on feature flags (DAT_680212ea, DAT_68021328, DAT_680213ad)\n10. For DAT_680213ad flag, retrieve secondary module base from DAT_68021122 and apply additional patches\n11. Call FUN_680233e9 to prepare secondary module, then install opcodes (0x8306b60f, 0x90907fe0, etc.)\n12. If DAT_680213f2 flag set, compute exponential progression table and install if successful\n13. Apply remaining conditional patches for DAT_68021425 and DAT_68021446 flags\n14. Install final function pointers and jump table entries for runtime hooks\n15. Call FUN_6802341d for post-patch validation and set completion flag DAT_68021486 = 1\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused1 - Unused parameter passed in ECX (legacy interface compatibility)\ndwUnused2 - Unused parameter passed in EDX (legacy interface compatibility)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects on loaded modules, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nAll patches are conditional based on global configuration flags\nBinary modification targets are hardcoded offsets from module base addresses\nFailure in ComputeExponentialProgressionTable prevents progression patch installation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x9090 (36496) - NOP instruction pair to disable existing code\n0x31 (49) - XOR opcode for register clearing patches  \n0x2c (44) - SUB opcode for arithmetic patches\n0xeb (235) - Short JMP opcode for control flow redirection\n0xe8 (232) - CALL opcode for function call patches\n0xd0 (208) - Shift opcode for bit manipulation patches\n0x8306b60f (0x0fb60683) - MOVZX instruction for zero-extend patches\n0x90907fe0 (0xe07f9090) - Mixed NOP and JLE instruction sequence\n0x83909090 (0x90909083) - Mixed ADD and NOP instruction sequence\n0x3909090 (0x90090939) - OR and NOP instruction sequence\n0x2f (47) - Byte copy count for code block transfer\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling - assumes all target addresses are valid\nComputeExponentialProgressionTable NULL return prevents progression patch application\nModule base address validation performed by called functions",
