      "comment": "Validates entity boundaries and processes entity operations if validation passes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source entity boundary by checking field at offset 0xa8 against global threshold\n2. Validate target entity boundary by checking field at offset 100 against configured limit\n3. Validate config parameter boundary by checking field at offset 0x14 against global threshold\n4. Return false immediately if any boundary validation fails\n5. Call entity callback function with target entity and callback address 0x68022bc5\n6. Check if unaffected EBP register value is below global threshold g_dwEbpThreshold\n7. If EBP condition fails, return false without processing\n8. Call FUN_68022ebf to get entity handle for source entity\n9. Call FUN_68022cec with entity handle offsets 0x24 and 0x28 for data processing\n10. Call FUN_68022c7b to perform entity-to-entity operation\n11. Update target entity field at offset 100 with sum of global value and source entity field\n12. Call completion callback function with global parameter g_dwCallbackParameter\n13. Return true indicating successful processing\n\nParameters:\npSourceEntity - Pointer to source GameEntity structure (accessed at offset 0xa8)\npTargetEntity - Pointer to target GameEntity structure (accessed at offset 100/0x64)\npValidationConfig - Pointer to ConfigData validation structure (accessed at offset 0x14)\nIMPLICIT EBP - Register parameter used for additional validation threshold check\n\nReturns:\ntrue - All validations passed and entity processing completed successfully\nfalse - Validation failed or EBP threshold check failed, no processing performed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSource entity boundary validation uses field at offset 0xa8 (168 decimal)\nTarget entity boundary validation uses field at offset 100 (0x64 hex)\nConfig validation uses field at offset 0x14 (20 decimal)\nEBP register provides additional runtime validation independent of parameters\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xa8 (168) - Source en