      "comment": "Enable server resource flags for registration handle during server initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call resource lookup function via g_pfnResourceLookupFunction with resource ID 0x86\n2. Check if resource object was successfully retrieved (non-NULL pointer)\n3. If resource found, set flag value 0xff at offset 0xe4 in resource structure\n4. Return original registration handle unchanged\n\nParameters:\ndwRegistrationHandle (uint) - Server registration handle from initialization process\n\nReturns:\nuint - Original registration handle passed through unchanged\n  Success: Same value as dwRegistrationHandle parameter\n  Function always returns input handle regardless of resource lookup result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If resource lookup fails (returns NULL), no flags are modified but function still succeeds\n- Resource ID 0x86 appears to be a specific server resource type identifier\n- Flag value 0xff at offset 0xe4 likely enables some server capability or feature\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x86 (134 decimal) - Resource type identifier for server resource lookup\n0xe4 (228 decimal) - Byte offset in resource structure for flag storage  \n0xff (255 decimal) - Flag value to enable server resource functionality\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error handling - function is designed to always succeed\n- NULL resource pointer is handled gracefully by skipping flag update\n- Registration handle is always returned as pass-through value",
