      "comment": "Generates pseudorandom number using linear congruential generator with modulo operation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Multiply accumulator low word by LCG constant 0x6ac690c5\n2. Add accumulator high word to create 64-bit intermediate result\n3. Extract high 32 bits and store back to accumulator high word\n4. Extract low 32 bits and store back to accumulator low word\n5. If modulus is non-zero, compute modulo result of low 32 bits\n6. Return combined 64-bit value: upper result in high word, modulo in low word\n\nParameters:\ndummy (dword): Unused parameter for calling convention alignment\nupperResult (dword): High 32-bit word of return value (passed through)\nmodulus (dword): Divisor for modulo operation, 0 disables modulo\npAccumulatorHigh (dword*): Pointer to high 32 bits of accumulator state\npAccumulatorLow (dword*): Pointer to low 32 bits of accumulator state\n\nReturns:\nulonglong: High 32 bits = upperResult parameter, Low 32 bits = modulo result or 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6ac690c5: LCG multiplier constant for pseudorandom generation\n0xffffffff: 32-bit mask for extracting low word before modulo\n0x20: Bit shift count for extracting high 32 bits\n\nSpecial Cases:\nmodulus == 0: Modulo operation skipped, returns 0 in low word\nAccumulator overflow: Handled naturally by 64-bit arithmetic",
