      "comment": "Initializes the Diablo II Warden anti-cheat system by loading library and setting up handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if warden system is already initialized (g_nWardenInitialized == 0)\n2. Verify warden is enabled via global flag (g_dwWardenEnabled != 0) \n3. Load d2warden.dll library using LoadLibraryA function pointer\n4. Store library handle in g_hWardenLibrary global variable\n5. Get d2warden_thread function address using GetProcAddress\n6. Store thread function pointer in g_pfnWardenThread global\n7. Get d2warden_0X66Handler function address using GetProcAddress\n8. Store 0x66 handler function pointer in g_pfnWarden66Handler global\n9. Get d2warden_0X68Handler function address using GetProcAddress  \n10. Store 0x68 handler function pointer in g_pfnWarden68Handler global\n11. If any function lookup fails, call FreeLibrary and cleanup\n12. If all functions found, create thread using CreateThread API\n13. Set g_nWardenInitialized to final initialization result\n14. Return QWORD combining original EAX register with second parameter\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused1 (ECX) - First parameter passed in ECX register but never used\ndwUnused2 (EDX) - Second parameter passed in EDX register, returned in high DWORD\nIMPLICIT dwOriginalEAX - Original EAX register value returned in low DWORD\n\nReturns:\nQWORD value where:\n- Low DWORD (bits 0-31): Original EAX register value\n- High DWORD (bits 32-63): dwUnused2 parameter value\nFunction itself returns success/failure via g_nWardenInitialized global\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If warden already initialized (g_nWardenInitialized != 0), function exits early\n- If warden disabled (g_dwWardenEnabled == 0), function exits early  \n- If DLL load fails, function exits early with failure\n- If any function address lookup fails, DLL is freed and globals reset\n- If thread creation fails, warden system remains disabled\n\nError Handling:\n- DLL load failure: Exit early, leave globals unchanged\n- Function lookup failure: Call FreeLibrary, reset g_dwWardenEnabled to 0\n- Thread creation failure: Reset g_dwWardenEnabled to 0, leave DLL loaded\n- All errors propagated via g_nWardenInitialized global flag\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x68023202 - g_nWardenInitialized global flag address\n0x68021288 - g_dwWardenEnabled global flag address  \n0x6802325d - g_hWardenLibrary HMODULE handle address\n0x6802320a - g_pfnWardenThread function pointer address\n0x6802320e - g_pfnWarden66Handler function pointer address\n0x68023212 - g_pfnWarden68Handler function pointer address\n0x68021142 - LoadLibraryA function pointer address\n0x6802111e - GetProcAddress function pointer address\n0x68021146 - FreeLibrary function pointer address  \n0x6802115e - CreateThread function pointer address\n0x68023216 - \"d2warden.dll\" string address\n0x68023223 - \"d2warden_thread\" string address\n0x68023233 - \"d2warden_0X66Handler\" string address\n0x68023248 - \"d2warden_0X68Handler\" string address",
