      "comment": "Conditionally dispatches a callback function based on global enable flag state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global callback enable flag (g_dwCallbackEnableFlag) for zero value\n2. If flag is zero (callbacks disabled), return early with concatenated parameters\n3. If flag is non-zero (callbacks enabled), preserve all registers with PUSHAD\n4. Call the registered callback function pointer (g_pfnCallbackFunction)\n5. Restore all registers with POPAD and clear EAX\n6. Return modified flags parameter shifted to high 32 bits\n\nParameters:\ndwControlParam - Control parameter passed through in concatenated return (ECX register)\ndwFlags - Flag/status parameter used in return value calculation (EDX register)\nIMPLICIT: dwInEax - Implicit EAX register input used in concatenation when callbacks disabled\n\nReturns:\nWhen callbacks disabled: Concatenated 64-bit value (dwFlags in high 32 bits, dwInEax in low 32 bits)\nWhen callbacks enabled: dwFlags shifted left 32 bits (high 32 bits only, low 32 bits cleared)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction uses __fastcall convention with ECX/EDX parameters\nPUSHAD/POPAD preserves all registers during callback execution\nCallback function pointer can be null (will cause crash if called when enabled)\n\nError Handling:\nNo validation performed on callback function pointer\nNo bounds checking on parameters\nCallback execution errors propagate to caller",
