      "comment": "Changes memory protection for a module section to PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE (0x20).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate PE header address from DOS header e_lfanew field\n2. Extract section size and virtual address from PE header fields\n3. Calculate absolute section address by adding virtual address to module base\n4. Call VirtualProtect via function pointer to change section protection\n5. Store old protection value in local variable (unused by caller)\n\nParameters:\ndwReserved - Reserved parameter, currently unused (value ignored)\nhModule - Handle to loaded module (base address for PE calculations)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return status (VirtualProtect result ignored)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function assumes valid PE module structure\n- No error handling if VirtualProtect fails\n- Old protection value stored but not used by calling function\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3c - Offset to e_lfanew field in DOS header (PE header location)\n0x1c - Offset to SizeOfCode in PE optional header \n0x2c - Offset to AddressOfEntryPoint in PE optional header\n0x20 - PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE protection flag for VirtualProtect\n\nError Handling:\n- No validation of module handle or PE structure integrity\n- VirtualProtect errors are not checked or propagated\n- Function assumes caller has validated module before calling",
