      "comment": "Sets the code section of a PE image to executable memory protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate NT header address by reading e_lfanew offset (pImageBase + 0x3c)\n2. Add pImageBase to get actual NT header location\n3. Read SizeOfCode field from optional header (NT header + 0x1c)\n4. Read BaseOfCode field from optional header (NT header + 0x2c)\n5. Calculate code section virtual address (BaseOfCode + pImageBase)\n6. Initialize dwOldProtect to 0 for VirtualProtect output\n7. Call VirtualProtect via function pointer to set PAGE_EXECUTE_READ (0x40)\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused (uint): Unused first parameter, purpose unknown\npImageBase (byte*): Base address of loaded PE image in memory\n\nReturns:\nint: VirtualProtect return value (non-zero for success, zero for failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nPE Header Magic Numbers:\n  0x3c - Offset to e_lfanew field in DOS header\n  0x1c - Offset to SizeOfCode in NT optional header  \n  0x2c - Offset to BaseOfCode in NT optional header\n  0x40 - PAGE_EXECUTE_READ memory protection constant\n\nError Handling:\nFunction relies on VirtualProtect error handling and returns its status directly.\nNo validation of PE header structure or memory addresses performed.",
