      "comment": "Modifies memory protection settings for critical sections of a loaded PE module\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse PE header to locate code section virtual address and size\n2. Calculate absolute address of code section using module base + virtual address  \n3. Call VirtualProtect to set code section as PAGE_EXECUTE_READ (0x20)\n4. Call VirtualProtect on hardcoded module offset 0xf8d68 with protection flags 2\n5. Store old protection values in stack variable for API requirements\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused - Unused parameter for interface compatibility (passed as 0)\npbModuleBase - Base address of loaded PE module to modify\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects on module memory protection\n\nSpecial Cases:\nHardcoded offset 0xf8d68 suggests specific data section targeting\nFunction uses indirect calls through DAT_6802117e (VirtualProtect function pointer)\nVirtualProtect calls made with different size parameters: section size vs fixed 0x6298\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3c (60) - PE header offset location in DOS header\n0x2c (44) - Virtual address field offset in section header  \n0x1c (28) - Size field offset in section header\n0x20 (32) - PAGE_EXECUTE_READ protection constant\n0xf8d68 (1019240) - Hardcoded offset for secondary protection change\n0x6298 (25240) - Fixed size for secondary VirtualProtect call\n2 (2) - Protection flags for secondary call (PAGE_READONLY)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes PE structure validity\nVirtualProtect failures not handled - relies on caller validation",
