      "comment": "Prepares code sections for binary patching by changing memory protection attributes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse PE header by reading e_lfanew offset (0x3c) from DOS header to locate NT headers\n2. Calculate NT headers address: nNtHeadersOffset = hModuleBase + *(hModuleBase + 0x3c)\n3. Extract section information from NT headers: VirtualSize at offset 0x1c, VirtualAddress at offset 0x2c\n4. Initialize old protection storage variable (dwOldProtection = 0) and get pointer to it\n5. Set new protection value to PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE (0x40) for code modification\n6. Call VirtualProtect on primary module section: address = hModuleBase + VirtualAddress, size = VirtualSize\n7. Call VirtualProtect on secondary module section: address = nSecondaryModuleBase + 0xf8d68, size = 0x6298\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused - Legacy parameter not used (compatibility with older interface)\nhModuleBase - Handle to primary module to prepare for patching\nIMPLICIT nSecondaryModuleBase in ESI - Base address of secondary module from caller context\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects on memory protection, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nVirtualProtect failures are not handled - assumes valid module addresses\nSecondary module base address comes from register ESI set by caller\nProtection changes apply to code sections only, not data sections\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3c (60) - Standard offset to e_lfanew field in IMAGE_DOS_HEADER\n0x1c (28) - Offset to VirtualSize field in IMAGE_SECTION_HEADER  \n0x2c (44) - Offset to VirtualAddress field in IMAGE_SECTION_HEADER\n0x40 (64) - PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE memory protection constant\n0xf8d68 (1019240) - Fixed offset for secondary module section start\n0x6298 (25240) - Fixed size of secondary module section to patch\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling for VirtualProtect failures\nAssumes all module pointers are valid and accessible\nNo validation of PE header structure integrity",
