      "comment": "TriggerRandomEvent - Conditionally triggers a random event based on probability threshold\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Generate random number from 0-1000 using global random number generator function\n2. Compare random value against global probability threshold (g_dwRandomEventThreshold)  \n3. If random value is below threshold AND entity has valid event handler (offset 0x80), proceed\n4. Call global event trigger handler function with entity handler, mode 1, and flag 1\n5. Return incremented value from global event counter\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\nIMPLICIT: ESI - Entity register/pointer to game object with event handler at offset 0x80\n\nReturns:\nint - Incremented value from global event counter (*g_pdwEventCounter + 1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If random value >= threshold, skips event triggering but still returns counter\n- If entity has no event handler (null at offset 0x80), skips event but still returns counter  \n- Function always returns incremented counter regardless of whether event was triggered\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3e8 (1000) - Maximum value for random number generation (range 0-1000)\n0x80 (128) - Byte offset within entity structure containing event handler function pointer\n0x0 (0) - Minimum value for random number generation\n0x1 (1) - Event mode parameter passed to trigger handler\n0x1 (1) - Event flag parameter passed to trigger handler",
