      "comment": "Computes exponential progression table for mathematical calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source data array existence and element count from global structure\n2. Allocate result table with element count * 0x38 bytes per entry via function pointer\n3. For each source element:\n   a. Check if element has non-zero weight value\n   b. If zero weight: Clear 7 table entries to zero\n   c. If non-zero weight:\n      - Calculate exponential decay factors for X and Y coordinates\n      - Generate 7 progression values using iterative multiplication\n      - Apply formula: (baseValue / (1.0 - factor^n)) * factor^n\n      - Round results and store in allocated table\n4. Return pointer to allocated progression table\n\nParameters:\n- None (IMPLICIT: uses global data structures for source data and allocation function)\n\nReturns:\n- uint *: Pointer to allocated progression table (caller must manage memory)\n- NULL: If source data invalid, element count zero, or memory allocation fails\n\nStructure Layout:\nProgressionSourceElement (44 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type     | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | nBaseValueX   | int      | Base X coordinate value\n+0x04  | 4    | nBaseValueY   | int      | Base Y coordinate value\n+0x08  | 4    | reserved1     | int      | Reserved field\n+0x0C  | 4    | nWeight       | int      | Weight value for progression calculation\n+0x10  | 28   | reserved2     | byte[28] | Additional element data\n\nProgressionResultEntry (56 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type     | Description\n+0x00  | 28   | adwXValues    | uint[7]  | 7 X progression values\n+0x1C  | 28   | adwYValues    | uint[7]  | 7 Y progression values\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x38 (56): Size of each result table entry (14 * 4-byte values)\n0x2C (44): Size of each source element structure\n0x1C (28): Offset to Y values in result entry\ng_flUnityConstant (1.0): Mathematical constant used in progression formula",
